Two facts opened this round. First: v6's league submission
settled — status PLACED, membership lpm_2c66cae — the
champion is competing in the division now. Second, Will's
direction: continue evolving, and apply Singular principles.

SINGULAR, APPLIED: foreign flavor comes from Singular,
never imports. The obvious move — trace the splash
builders' deck (T11) and copy it — is an import. Rejected.
v7 is authored from our own verified claims and the pool's
mechanics, derived here before any episode ran:

  * T7 (ours): face pressure wins games. The win condition
    is hero damage; everything prices against it.
  * The Warrior precon is FLAT — 4 copies of all ten cards,
    no curve, no trinkets. In a pool capped at 4 copies,
    composition edges are small by construction (one reason
    the pilots' tribe wins on decisions, U5b).
  * The discount mechanic, read natively: a class trinket
    in play cuts the off-class surcharge by 1. Bolt (Archer,
    1-cost, 2 damage to anything) is the pool's cheapest
    face reach; under 2+ Archer trinkets it costs 1-2 and
    reaches past any board to the hero — reach the Warrior
    width engine lacks when its swings are blocked by
    bodies.
  * Banner is the width engine (a free Footsoldier every
    turn); Swords/Shields multiply width. Keep the engine,
