Round 33 - The Floors, Refreshed: the Rado Replica Finds His Focus (EE 762-769)
Run the same day as the oracle loop's partial (1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.35), on Will's direction in chat: "don't wait, immediately iterate." This round performs the loop's two skipped legs - replica refresh against the fresh traces, and playtest + adapt - in full. SCREEN-class and league-harvest evidence only: no registry transitions, nothing uploaded, nothing submitted, no xp-requests launched.

STEP 1 - TRACING THE FRESH CORPUS: all 273 champion-seated episodes from the EE 709-713 harvest were traced with tracer29v3 on the hub: 273/273 episodes, 30,605/30,605 per-tick state hashes matched - the decoding is exact, the Round 29 standard. The corpus is now fully traced at 507 champion episodes (234 + 273). Profiles recomputed per cohort (cac-dist/top2/analyze33.py -> profiles33.json); combined corpus: rado 345 games, macroMage 236, macroWarrior 109.
WHAT MOVED - RADO: almost nothing, and that is the finding. Same fixed deck. Pillage +1-power branch 144/144 in the new cohort (290/290 combined). Tactician at the max-power enemy 0.88 (was 0.87). Hail: 76 new plays, enemy-board min 5, p25 11, median 15 (old: 71 plays, min 6, median 15). Dies first in 6.0% of new games (old 5.6%) - still the field's best survival. Win/loss tick split even again (112.0 / 113.5) - "his wins run long" refuted a second time. His cohort win share: 0.414 (Round 29 window) -> 0.377 (new window), combined 0.394, against a season rate of 0.343: the windows differ by field mix, not by a new rado.
WHAT MOVED - THE FOCUS MEASUREMENT: hero attacks at the lowest-life enemy fell 0.770 (old) -> 0.692 (new) - an 8-sigma drop that is NOT a behaviour change. A grid search over scored targeting rules finds his rule in both cohorts: minimize life - 2*boardPower + boardCount agrees 0.816 (old) / 0.784 (new), 0.799 combined over 3,884 hero attacks, against pure-lowest's 0.770 / 0.692. He discounts a target by its board power; the new fields carry bigger boards, so the discount bites more often and the pure-lowest metric sagged. Round 29's "77% at the lowest-life enemy" was the scored rule seen through smaller fields.
WHAT MOVED - MACRO: the deck-selection weights shifted: C2 Mage hybrid 58.7% of his games (Round 29 window) -> 52.1% (new), combined 55.1%; C1 (Warrior, Bubble-for-Duel) 12.3% -> 14.7% new; Mage fraction of his games 71.0% -> 66.3%. His Warrior families' corpus win share collapsed 0.378 -> 0.219 while their measured play is unchanged (lowest-frac 0.727 -> 0.743, plays/turn 1.23 -> 1.25) - a field effect, not a play change. He dies first more often: 11.6% -> 14.2%. The Mage disciplines are absolute in both cohorts: Post played only with a minion in hand 182/182 new (337/337 combined, mean 2.70-2.78 minions in hand), minion plays under a live Post 0.944, every Sharpshooter ping at a hero 533/0 new (1,052/0 combined).
REPLICA REFRESH (cac-dist/top2/fidelity33.py): rado-replica's focus is now the scored rule; macro-replica draws combos at the combined weights (C2 55, C3 13, C4 10, C1 14, C5 8). F1 validation - 240 recorded matches on Round 29's seed plan with the refreshed replicas, traced 240/240, 31,279/31,279 hashes: rado-replica 105 wins (43.8% of the room), macro-replica 19 (7.9%), v11 51, v16 42, v17-value 23. VERDICTS, replacing Round 29's stale ones: (1) RADO FLOOR - STRONGER, high behavioral fidelity. His F1 room share rose 26.2% -> 43.8%, at his combined corpus strength (0.394); the replica's observable lowest-life fraction is 0.741 against the real 0.729 - Round 29's named focus divergence (replica 1.000) is CLOSED. Action mix .46/.31/.23 against his .44/.32/.23; plays/turn 1.24 vs 1.28. Remaining divergences, named: scored agreement 1.000 by construction against his 0.799 (his rule carries residual variation no single score captures), F1 ticks 130.3 vs 113.1 (the F1 room runs long). (2) MACRO FLOOR - slightly stronger overall (room share 4.6% -> 7.9%), discipline fidelity high, strength fidelity STILL LOW for the Mage family: F1 family win share 0.036 against his real 0.403 - the replica's flood still does not convert locally (Round 29's verdict stands for Mage); the Warrior family is closer (0.173 vs 0.284). The macro floor remains a floor, not a portrait. (3) Caveat measured in both F1 recordings: the replica's combo draws cluster on our seed plans (C2 drew 147/240 in Round 29's F1 and 147/240 again in Round 33's, under different thresholds) - the engine RNG's first draw on seeded plans is not uniform; deck-draw fidelity is seed-plan-dependent.

STEP 2 - THE LINE, RE-MEASURED (Run A: preflight 558 s, run 61 s for 63,600 matches = 1,043 matches/s run-phase, the fastest recorded; fleet 16/18, rock-mountain and halycon-vector excluded at preflight). Every comparison below carries the refreshed-floor caveat: the floors moved, so the marks are not commensurable with Round 32's except where stated. CF (refreshed): rado-replica 43.9% (was 23.5 against the old floor), v11 20.3 (was 27.6), v16 15.4 (was 29.7), v17-value 10.6, macro-replica 9.8. CF3 composition: rado-replica 43.3, v22-hail 20.0 - Round 32's CF3 mark of 42.1 DOES NOT HOLD against the refreshed floor. League-shaped L22: rado-replica 60.8 (was 40.8), macro-replica 15.0, warrior 14.9, v22-hail 6.4 - Round 32's 19.7 DOES NOT HOLD either. CORRECTION TO ROUND 32's VERDICT, in the open: its "one hunk closed roughly a fifth of the gap" was measured against the soft floor and is withdrawn; against a behaviorally calibrated rado the league-shaped gap is ~26 points (6.4% against the 0.327 bar), not ~20. The refresh, not the line, moved - v22 did not get worse tonight; our measurement of the opposition got honest.

STEP 3 - CANDIDATE v23-hail12 (bots/v23-hail12.bas): v22 with ONE constant changed - the Hail gate rises from 8 to 12 total enemy minions. Justification from the traces: Round 32 acquitted the blast cost but never tested the gate's timing, and the refreshed corpus prices his patience exactly - 147 Hail plays across both cohorts at enemy boards min 5, p25 11, median 15, p75 20; v21 imported the swap at the replica's looser threshold (8), not his. Hail is a 6-energy off-class spell and this deck's only board-clear; at 8 total minions across four opponents it fires before the flood peaks (macroMage board peak 12.0). GATE 1 (Divergence): SIGHTED - 2.16% winner-seat divergence over 2,040 paired cells, zero missing. The gate change is real but touches few games. GATE 2 (Run B attempt 2: preflight 607 s, run 120 s, 106,000 matches, 883 matches/s, fleet 16/18): gauntlet subject pooled 9.9% (GC 9.1, GD 10.7) against v22's 9.8 - unchanged, and this comparison IS floor-independent (GC/GD seat no replicas). CF3: v23 19.8% against v22's 20.0 in the same composition, same round, refreshed floors - a wash. CF2: v23 14.9% (rado-replica 46.3 atop the table). League-shaped L23: v23 6.5% against v22's 6.4 - a wash. VERDICT: v23-hail12 is at parity with its parent on every surface; the 2.16% of games the gate retimes split evenly. NOT an advance - v22-hail remains the advancing line and the next build's parent, and the Hail gate is now acquitted on timing as Round 32 acquitted it on blast. The remaining gap does not live in this constant.

DISTANCE TO THE BAR: league-shaped best lineage mark 6.5% (v23) / 6.4% (v22) against the bar 0.327 (macromackie's league mean_score, EE 709) - roughly a fifth of the bar, ~26 points short. The rado floor's 60.4-60.8% in that table is a floor-model share in a field holding two stock references; the real rado's corpus share is 0.394 in stronger league fields - the floor is calibrated to his behaviour and F1 strength, not to that table's arithmetic. v16 remains the seated league champion; the submission hold stands, on stronger evidence than it stood on this morning. MOAT: no registry transitions - all of this round's evidence is local/SCREEN-class or league harvest already recorded; counts unchanged (True 14, False 7, Unknown 15, Fiction 2).

MACHINERY AND INCIDENTS, named: (1) Run B attempt 1 failed in preflight with ALL 18 nodes excluded and aborted before the clock - zero matches played, nothing double-counted. The identical preflight steps, run manually against an excluded node minutes later, passed end to end (ssh, scp, binary hash 13545c71...): a transient transport failure through the shared egress proxy at its contended worst, not a roster or hash defect. Attempt 2 completed the full run. (2) The first Gate 1 dispatch silently produced no results: a sed-generated dispatch script kept the old node-probe filename (the pattern missed 'probe32' inside 'node-probe32.sh'), so shards wrote results under the old name and the collection step found nothing. Caught by the empty return, fixed, re-dispatched - 2,040/2,040 cells, zero missing. (3) All Round 33 runs executed from a hash-pinned snapshot tree (cac-dist/r33/, round.sh sha256 05f3d8c1); round.sh was not edited while any run lived. Round totals: 173,920 matches screened (63,600 Run A + 106,000 Run B + 4,080 divergence-probe arms + 240 F1 recordings).
CORRECTION (amendment to the Round 32 scroll, 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.34): that scroll calls rock-mountain's Round 32 exclusion "its fourth straight preflight failure." The strictly verifiable statement is narrower: rock-mountain was excluded in all three of Round 32's runs (four attempts counting Run C's two), and in every recorded attempt since Round 30's Run B except Round 31's Run B, whose preflight roster was not verified. The ordinal in the Round 32 scroll is an undercount under any reading and is superseded by this note. (For the current record: rock-mountain was also excluded in both of Round 33's completed runs.)
Weakness Audit - The Spared Executioner: the Champions' Unexplored Weaknesses, Ranked (EE 770)
On Will's direction in chat: "find their unexplored weaknesses." Analysis only, over the fully-traced champion corpus - 507 episodes, every per-tick state hash validated (rado 345 games, macroMage 236, macroWarrior 109). Scripts and raw aggregates: cac-dist/top2/audit.py, audit2.py, audit3.py, audit.json, audit2.json; working copy at cac-dist/top2/weakness-register.md. No fleet screens, nothing uploaded, nothing submitted, no xp-requests. Ranked by evidence strength x exploitability by a BASIC policy in our lineage; every claim carries n and its field-mix falsifier. Corpus frame: fields are 4-5 players; NO Archer-class player exists in the corpus (2,264 seat-slots: Warrior 1,221, Mage 1,043) - every Hail in this meta is carried by a Warrior deck. In 183 games seating both champions: rado won 67, macro 48, the field 68.

W1 - THE SPARED EXECUTIONER (both champions; the register's top claim). A clean missed lethal = the champion ends a turn with unspent can-attack board power >= the lowest living enemy's life, that enemy holding no Bubble (Bubble bounces the first attacker; the control barely moves the count - 13/315 rado and 11/256 macroMage raw events were Bubble-protected). rado: 140 clean events across 100 of his 209 losses (47.8%); in 48 losses (23.0%) the spared lowest player later landed the killing blow on rado himself. macroMage: 116 clean events across 85 of 141 losses (60.3%); the spared player killed him in 46 losses (32.6%). macroWarrior: 49 clean events in 37 of 78 losses (47.4%), spared-killer in 19 (24.4%). Median ticks from a missed lethal to the champion's death in losses: 15 (rado), 16.5 (macroMage). FALSIFIER, stated: FFA sparing is often correct - missed-lethal events also occur in wins (rado 168 win-events vs 147 loss-events) and killing the lowest can feed the leader. The claim is narrowed to the tail the falsifier cannot explain: sparing a player who then kills YOU, 23-33% of all champion losses. EXPLOIT: be the player they spare. Rado's scored rule (life - 2*boardPower + boardCount) already ranks a low-life, wide-board player last; the audit says the leak persists past the rule - their end-turn discipline does not convert residual power into finishes. Single hunk on the v24/v22 line: when our hero life <= 8, sequence plays body-first and value board count over board polish in that band. Compounds Round 34's sling rather than competing with it; measure it where it lives (our deaths-at-low-life-with-board rate; champions' kill-share on us when we are lowest).

W2 - RADO'S HAIL GATE PRICES 1-TOUGH KILLS; AN UNDAMAGED WARRIOR BOARD IS IMMUNE. His 147 traced fires, by enemy 1-tough body count at fire time: min 3, p10 6, p25 9, median 11, p75 15, max 27. On 913 turns where he held Hail with >= 3 energy unplayed, held 1-tough counts ran median 7, and 367 holds sat at >= 9 - inside his fire band: the gate is a soft band centred ~9-11 kills, not a cliff (consistent with Round 33's gate-12 parity: the gate is not a constant). Underneath: Hail kills only 1-tough bodies, and the stock Warrior board is printed entirely at toughness >= 2 (Footsoldier 1/2, Bear 3/2, Tactician 1/2, Commander 2/3). Against an undamaged Warrior board his 4 Hail copies kill nothing - and he died holding at least one Hail in 122 of 209 losses (58%), mean hand at death 4.9 cards. FALSIFIER: died-holding alone would be base rate (4 copies, big hands); the load-bearing evidence is the fire-band distribution - he demonstrably waits for 1-tough mass a Warrior board never presents until pre-damaged. EXPLOIT: deny the band - Shields (+0/+1) targeting preference to our most-damaged minion, restoring bodies to toughness >= 2, and prefer clean trades over leaving 1-tough remnants. Corollary: in the turns right after we play fresh bodies, his Hail is at its deadest - press attacks then.

W3 - MACRO'S FLOOD IS POST-WINDOWED; HIS LOSSES ARE HALF-BUILT FLOODS. macroMage bodies fielded per game: 23.8 in wins vs 12.5 in losses. Turns ending with >= 3 energy unspent: 30.8% of loss turns (246/798) vs 18.5% of win turns (104/563). He dies holding unplayed shooters - Sharpshooter 122 + Sniper 113 card instances across 141 losses (~1.7 per loss) - and a Post in hand in 38/141 losses (27%). The mechanism is his own discipline: 95.1% of minion plays occur under a live Post and Post lasts 2 turns, so his output has hard windows and outside them he passes with energy in hand. FALSIFIER: reverse causality is partly real (losing positions offer fewer good plays); the discipline numbers bound it - the Post-gating is a policy constant present in wins too; losses are the games where the windows never opened or were answered. EXPLOIT: fire our Hail into the window, not at the board count. The v22 gate (>= 8 total enemy bodies) trips late against macro because his board crosses 8 exactly during a Post window, as 1-tough copied shooters. Single hunk: when any opposing Post is live, our Hail gate drops to >= 5 enemy bodies with >= 3 of them 1-tough.

W4 - MACRO'S BURNOUT CLOCK (narrow but verified). 11 of macroMage's 141 losses (7.8%) end on his own end-of-turn trigger: Burnout deals the final 2 with his life at 1-4, Burnout on his board - verified on the killing actions' events (3 of 3 sampled identical in shape). Where Burnout was aboard at death it had appeared a median 32 ticks earlier (n=96): 2 damage + a forced toss on every one of his end-of-turns. FALSIFIER APPLIED, claim narrowed: Burnout PRESENCE is acquitted - aboard at the final state in 54% of his wins (68/126) vs 44% at death in losses (96/219). The weakness is only the endgame band: at life <= 4 with Burnout aboard he finishes himself; damage into him there is worth half unless it kills this turn (aim-rule discount, one hunk).

W5 - SIGNATURE MATCHUPS. Win share by opposing deck signature present (per-opponent-seat cells): macroMage 0.313 vs radoDeck (n=233) vs 0.441 vs stockWarrior (238), 0.448 vs stockMage (125), 0.396 vs macroDeck (235); macroWarrior 0.229 vs radoDeck (n=109), his worst split; rado 0.358 in radoDeck mirrors (n=162) vs 0.388-0.409 against every other signature. Indirect but real exploitability: our lineage IS a radoDeck - 507 hosted games confirm the shape is macro's worst matchup and rado's worst field is a second rado. Keep the Hail package; price league fields by signature mix, not class labels.

W6 - RADO COLLAPSES: SUDDENLY, TO WIDTH, USUALLY TO MAGE FLOOD. In 111 of 209 losses (53%) rado was at life >= 10 ten ticks before death (median 10). His killers' boards at the killing blow: median 10 bodies, 16 total power, best single body 3 - width, not height; 199/209 kills are minion attacks; loss-winners are Mage-class in 128/209 (61%). His own bodies/game: 13.6 in wins vs 9.0 in losses. EXPLOIT SKETCH: the shape that kills him is a one-turn alpha from a wide board, not incremental trades - a hold-and-alpha override (board count >= 8 and rado's life <= our total board power: commit all attacks to his hero that turn). FALSIFIER: killer-board medians are dominated by macro floods; a Warrior board reaching 8-10 bodies is rarer, which is also why the override is cheap to carry.

W7 - MACRO'S CLASS LOTTERY (variance knowledge, not a hunk). macroMage 0.403 over 236 games; macroWarrior 0.284 over 109. By combo: C2 0.411 (n=190), C3 0.370 (46), C1 0.298 (47), C4 0.235 (34), C5 0.321 (28 - small-n flag). A third of macro's games start ~12 points down by draw. Not exploitable by our policy (we do not choose his draw; the replicas already draw at corpus weights) - but it corrects the bar: macro's league mean (0.327) understates his Mage form (0.403); distance-to-bar accounting against 0.327 prices his average draw, not his strong one.

W8 - RADO'S LATE-SEAT PENALTY IN 5-PLAYER FIELDS (field knowledge). 5p only, rado by seat position: seats 0-1 combined 0.456 (36/79), seats 2-3 combined 0.254 (16/63), seat 4 0.345 (10/29); flat in 4p (0.357-0.478). Cells 29-41 games, moderate-n flagged. No exploit - seats are dealt; it predicts his league share varies with seat draw.

W9 - MACRO'S PING RULE: PRICED, AND ACQUITTED. The 1,052/0 hero-only ping rule costs almost nothing measurable: the creature that eventually killed macroMage had been ping-spared in only 7 of his 141 losses (5.0%), and spared 1-tough creatures dealt a mean 0.06 later hero-damage per spared instance (7,900 instances, 449 total). A negative result, recorded so nobody re-hunts it: do not spend a hunk baiting his pings.

W10 - OPENING BOOK: NO WEAKNESS FOUND. Damage taken in the first 10 ticks averages 0.03-0.19 for both champions in wins and losses alike - the opening is bloodless. First-turn minion is flat for rado (0.402 with, n=169; 0.386 without, n=176) and mildly positive for macroWarrior (0.321 vs 0.250, n=53/56 - small-n flag). No hunk.

METHOD NOTE: missed-lethal here is computable lethal only (residual can-attack power vs lowest enemy life at end of turn; card-based lethal such as Bolt is not counted), so the true leak is at least this large. MOAT: no registry transitions - this audit is traced-corpus (SCREEN/harvest-class) evidence; counts unchanged (True 14, False 7, Unknown 15, Fiction 2). AIM THE NEXT BUILD AT W1: the largest n in the register (222 clean loss-events across both champions' families; the spared-killer tail alone covers 113 losses), shared by both champions, compounding the lines already in flight.
Round 34 - David vs Goliath: the Sling, Tested at the Mechanism (EE 770-774)

THE THESIS (Will's direction in chat: "David vs Goliath"): we do not out-tune the giants - three rounds (28, 30, 33) proved their edge is joint tuning bought with 64 and 166 versions. The sling is asymmetry. rado's targeting rule is known in closed form from 3,884 traced hero attacks (Round 33): he attacks the living enemy minimizing life - 2*boardPower + boardCount, a deterministic function of public state - and a deterministic function can be mispriced on purpose. The instrument finally supports the test: the refreshed rado-replica implements that rule and validates at high fidelity (focus 0.741 vs his 0.729; F1 room share 43.8% at corpus strength). SCREEN-class evidence only: no registry transitions, nothing uploaded, nothing submitted, no xp-requests launched.

THE CANDIDATE - v24-sling (bots/v24-sling.bas): ONE hunk from v22-hail, in the card-play loop. v22 visits the hand from a random starting position; v24 builds a visit order (ord()) first: minions before everything, ascending power then cost (key power*16 + cost: Footsoldier 17, Tactician 18, Commander 37, Bear 50), non-minions keeping v22's random rotation behind them. The function's arithmetic is the justification: every minion we play moves our score by 1 - 2*itsPower - a Footsoldier or Tactician (power 1) costs 1 point, a Commander (power 2, summoning two Footsoldiers on entry) costs 5 for THREE bodies, a Bear (power 3) costs 5 for ONE body. Whenever energy forces a choice, the wide cheap bodies land before the tall ones, and the board rado prices on his turns is as expensive to attack as this deck can make it. Aim, swing, the Hail gate, teamcalc (partner -1), toss and triggers are v22 verbatim; the deck is unchanged (the Warrior minion pool is saturated at 4 copies each - no wider deck exists to swap to).

GATE 1 (Divergence): SIGHTED - 62.79% winner-seat divergence over 2,040 paired cells, zero missing: the widest candidate reading since v19-flood (69.23%). The ordering is no pricing ghost; it moves most games. What it moves them WITH is what Step 2 was built to ask.

STEP 2 - THE MECHANISM, MEASURED (the round's headline instrument): 300 recorded league-shaped matches per arm on the IDENTICAL seed plan (seeds 800000+m, R = m % 5), traced 600/600 with 90,468/90,468 per-tick state hashes matched. The replica's own target was the scored argmin in 100.0% of 9,147 hero attacks - the instrument is exact, so the metric reads the mechanism, not the noise. rado-replica hero attacks: 4,550 in v24's games, 4,597 in v22's. On OUR hero: 1,331 (29.3%) against v24, 1,318 (28.7%) against v22. Our seat WAS his scored argmin at 30.1% of his attack moments against v24, 29.9% against v22. Our mean score rank at his attacks: 1.37 (v24) vs 1.43 (v22) of ~4 living enemies. THE STONE DID NOT FLY: his fire was not redirected - if anything a hair more of it lands on the shaped board (0.6 points on ~4,500 attacks per arm, ~0.6 sigma: parity). We remain his rule's FIRST-ranked target in both arms. (Recording win shares, n=300: v24 5.3%, v22 7.3% - inside noise; the 21,200-match league-shaped tables below arbitrate, and they say parity too.)

GATE 2 (refreshed floors throughout; Run A: preflight 733 s, run 100 s, 106,000 matches at 1,060 matches/s, fleet 16/18; Run B: preflight 564 s, run 96 s, 106,000 at 1,104 matches/s, fleet 16/18; zero chunk retries in 390 chunks). Table CF, fifth reproduction of the post-refresh field: rado-replica 44.6, v11 20.1, v16 15.1, v17-value 10.1, macro-replica 10.0. CF2: v24-sling 16.6 (rado 43.8, v11 19.7). CF3: v24-sling 21.7 (rado 41.5, v16 17.5, v17-value 12.2, macro 7.1) - the best post-refresh CF3 mark (v22 20.0, v23 19.8, both Round 33, cross-round). LEAGUE-SHAPED, the headline, same round and identical seed plan: L24 v24-sling 6.6 (rado 61.1, macro 14.9, warrior 14.3, archer 3.1); L22 v22-hail 6.7 (rado 60.4, macro 15.1, warrior 14.8, archer 2.9). PARITY - and the cost side is clean: no seat in the field moved more than 0.7 points between the two tables; the shaping neither bleeds nor buys in the composition it was built for. GAUNTLET (Run B; Table G re-measured: v17-value 62.0, v16 14.2, v11 13.1, warrior 8.1, archer 2.6): subject pooled, same round, same plan - v24-sling 10.3 (GC 9.5, GD 11.2) against v22-hail 9.9 (GC 9.0, GD 10.9). A +0.4 edge, inside the line's standing 9.5-10.6 band; the reference-field liability is unchanged.

VERDICT: the sling thesis is REFUTED at the mechanism level, and the candidate is at parity on the surface it was built for. v24-sling does NOT displace its parent: v22-hail remains the advancing line and the next build's parent. The two favorable secondary marks (CF3 21.7; gauntlet +0.4 same-round) are recorded as unexplained residuals, NOT as the sling working - the mechanism they would be attributed to is the one the traces just falsified; they are likelier sequencing side-effects of the reordering (Tactician timing, Hail affordability) in lineage-seated fields, and a future round may attribute or dissolve them. WHY THE STONE MISSED, from first principles: (1) the life term dominates - our seat runs a life deficit in champion fields (it dies first most often), his rule prices life 1:1, and the board differential the ordering can create is a few points on energy-scarce turns only; (2) end-of-turn boards converge - within a turn the same affordable cards are played in some order, so rado mostly prices the same board v22 presents, and the hunk's 62.79% divergence lives in sequencing, not in the board he prices; (3) the board LEVEL that could move his price - several points, sustained at his decision moments - is reachable only by fielding a weaker board in total: the asymmetry does not exist at a scale this deck can express. What the round proved positively: the instrument chain (closed-form rule -> replica -> paired trace metric at 100% instrument agreement) can falsify a mechanism in ONE round, before shares are even read. That is the David-sized weapon that survives this round: not the sling, but the aim.

DISTANCE TO THE BAR: league-shaped best lineage mark ~6.6-6.7% (v24 6.6, v22 6.7, this round) against the bar 0.327 (macromackie's league mean_score, EE 709) - ~26 points short, unchanged. v16 remains the seated league champion; the submission hold stands. MOAT: no registry transitions - all evidence local/SCREEN-class; counts unchanged (True 14, False 7, Unknown 15, Fiction 2).

MACHINERY AND INCIDENTS, named: all runs executed from the hash-pinned snapshot tree (cac-dist/r34/, round.sh sha256 05f3d8c1, carried unchanged from Round 33 - no machinery edits this round, and none under a live run). Preflight remains the pipeline's largest block (733 s / 564 s, serial session establishment through the shared egress proxy); the run phases - 1,060 and 1,104 matches/s - are the two fastest recorded, and zero of 390 chunks needed a retry. Fleet 16/18 in both runs: halycon-vector and rock-mountain excluded at preflight (rock-mountain's exclusion streak continues; the Round 33 correction's verifiable form stands). The mechanism recordings ran on the local v3 build (cac-headless-v3) and were traced on the hub with tracer29v3 - the Round 29 finding (sim/baseset byte-identical v3<->HEAD) is what licenses local recordings as evidence about the fleet game. The progress chart (cac-dist/progress-chart.html, generator make_progress_chart.py) is extended through Round 34 in the post-break era. Round totals: 216,680 matches screened (4,080 divergence-probe arms + 106,000 Run A + 106,000 Run B + 600 mechanism recordings).
Round 35 - The Spared Executioner, Tested: Be the Player They Spare (EE 809-816)
On Will's direction in chat: "iterate." The aim is the weakness audit's W1 (scroll 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.37): both champions end turns with clean lethals unspent on the lowest living enemy in 47.8% (rado) / 60.3% (macroMage) of their losses, and the spared lowest player personally killed them in 23.0% / 32.6% of those losses. The register's exploit shape: be the player they spare - low life + wide board, body-first sequencing at life <= 8. Round 34's discipline binds: the mechanism metrics were defined in analyze35.py's header, with the decision rule, before any tally existed.

THE BUILD - v25-spared (bots/v25-spared.bas), ONE hunk on v22-hail. In the card-play loop, when our hero's life is <= 8, a visit order is built in ord() - key = the round's random-rotation offset, plus 1000 for every non-minion card (handKind <> 0) - so in the band every body in hand is visited, and played subject to the unchanged affordability and copy-cap rules, before any non-body line. Above 8 the order is v22's rotation exactly: same random call, same sequence, the hunk silent. This is the register's prescription taken literally ("sequence plays body-first and value board count over board polish in that band") as a pure sequencing change - no pricing element, nothing priced. Verbatim from v22: aim, swing and trigger logic, the Hail package and its >= 8-body gate, teamcalc with partner forced to -1, the toss, the deck. Smoke-tested clean on cac-headless-v3 (league-shaped table and a 5x v25 table, no player errors).

DECISION RULE, stated before the tallies: v25 works iff (a) the champions' hero-fire share on our seat while we are strictly lowest AND (b) our death rate while lowest with a board both fall vs v22 beyond paired noise, AND the league-shaped share does not fall. (c) - the spared tail turned on them - moving alone is a tail-only result, not an advance.

GATE 1 - SIGHTED. 206 of 2,040 paired probe cells diverge (10.10%, zero missing; fleet of 6 probe nodes, seeds 750000-750407). The band hunk is behaviorally visible: it is reached and it changes play.

MECHANISM - 600 traced league-shaped matches (300 per arm, identical seed plans 800000+, rado-replica + macro-replica + warrior + archer refs; hashes 45,259 v25 + 45,274 v22, every hash matched). (a) Champion hero attacks while we are strictly lowest: 1,794 in each arm, on our hero 1,708 in each - 95.2% both. (a2) Our deaths while lowest: 270 (v25) / 271 (v22); killed by a champion 92.6% both. (b) Ever strictly-lowest with >= 1 body: 280 games each arm; we die in 268 (95.7%) vs 269 (96.1%) - one game. (c) Spared events (a champion ends his turn with unspent can-attack power >= our life while we are his lowest living enemy): rado 111 + macro 77 (v25) vs rado 108 + macro 77 (v22); we later land that champion's killing blow in 3 games vs 2. THE HUNK FIRES: ever-lowest with a WIDE board (>= 3 bodies) rises 224 -> 238 games - body-first demonstrably puts the register's profile on the table. THE SPARING DOES NOT FOLLOW: (a), (a2) and (b) are flat to the unit, (c) is noise. The reading, plainly: in the replica room, death at lowest is overdetermined - two corpus-strength replicas and the references all hold fire on the lowest seat (95%+ die once lowest, in both arms), so no single champion's end-turn discipline is the binding constraint on our survival; and W1's tail pays only a seat strong enough to execute the champion afterward - at a 7.7% / 7.3% recorded win share in this room, ours is not. The audit's numbers are hosted-field numbers, where ONE champion holds the lethal while the rest of the field cannot finish, and its denominator is champion losses; this test's denominator is our deaths. Round 35 bounds W1's exploitability by our line at our strength - it does not refute the audit. W1 re-opens when our seat is strong enough to punish a sparing (after W2/W3-class gains) or in hosted fields.

GATE 2 - refreshed floors, 21,200 matches per table. League-shaped (headline): L25 v25 6.5% vs L22 v22 6.6%, same round, same seed plan - parity. CF3: v25 19.5% (v22 20.0 in Round 33). CF2: v25 14.6%. Table CF baseline, sixth reproduction: rado-replica 43.9, v11 20.5, v16 15.2, v17-value 10.3, macro-replica 10.2. Cost side (gauntlet, floor-independent): subject pooled v25 9.9% vs v22's same-round 10.2% (GC 9.0 vs 9.2, GD 10.9 vs 11.1) - the survival shape bleeds nothing beyond the series' noise band; Table G reproduced again (62.3 / 13.9 / 13.5 / 7.7 / 2.6). VERDICT: v25-spared does not meet the decision rule - (a) and (b) flat, league-shaped parity, cost side parity. A parity variant, shelved beside v23; v22-hail remains the advancing line and the next build's parent. What survives: the ranked next hunks are W2 (deny rado's Hail band - Shields to the most-damaged minion, clean trades) and W3 (Post-window Hail gate), which act on the champions' gates rather than on our survival shape; and the trace instrument chain falsified a second mechanism in one round, before shares were read. DISTANCE TO THE BAR: league-shaped best remains 6.6% (v22) against the #1's league mean_score 0.327 - about 26 points, unchanged for the third straight round. v16 stays seated; the submission hold stands. MOAT: no registry transitions - all Round 35 evidence is SCREEN-class local play; counts unchanged (True 14, False 7, Unknown 15, Fiction 2).

RECONCILIATION - the contested coordinate 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.37, established by direct inspection of the builder, the built file, and the two stream commits. (1) The weakness audit (EE 770) and Round 34 (EE 770-774) were inscribed by two agents into the same builder as two assignments under the IDENTICAL dict key C(1,1,1, 1,1,1, 1,1,37) - the audit's at builder line 1466, Round 34's at line 1492. SCROLLS is a Python dict: the second assignment silently overwrote the first, and the builder's scroll-guard iterates the already-collided dict, so neither build could see the loss. (2) The audit's stream (commit 43dcc6c, 151,715 bytes) contained the audit scroll at .37 and no Round 34 scroll; Round 34's stream (commit 82b5de7, 150,004 bytes) contained Round 34's scroll at .37, both index lines - and no audit body (verified: audit body markers 0 in that blob, Round 34 markers present; in 43dcc6c the reverse). Each agent's remote verification passed because each verified its own scroll, not the other's. (3) The "remote matches neither local build" flag was a units artifact: the builder prints character counts - the audit's 151,109 chars = 151,715 bytes, Round 34's 149,396 chars = 150,004 bytes (608 bytes of multibyte UTF-8). No third build exists. (4) REPAIR, applied this round: the audit keeps .37 (first inscribed, first streamed; the home index lines are corrected to match and reordered), Round 34 is renumbered to .38 in the builder, this scroll sits at .39. The audit's full text survived intact in the builder source and in commit 43dcc6c - nothing was lost, only mis-keyed. Post-repair build verified locally before streaming: audit body markers present (1x each), Round 34 body present, file 159,491 bytes before this scroll.

MACHINERY AND INCIDENTS, named: (1) This VM was replaced mid-round; Run A attempt 1 died in preflight at 11/18 nodes with zero matches played and was relaunched from the hash-pinned snapshot (cac-dist/r35/, round.sh sha256 05f3d8c1, unedited) into a fresh out dir - nothing double-counted. (2) The first Gate 1 dispatch repeated Round 33's filename defect in mirror image: the sed that generated dispatch-probe35.sh missed 'node-probe34.sh' (the pattern '34probe' does not occur inside 'node-probe34'), so the shards ran Round 34's node script and wrote results34probe.txt while collection looked for results35probe.txt. Caught by the empty return, fixed, re-dispatched: 2,040/2,040 cells. The defect has now occurred in Rounds 33 and 35 by two generation paths; the process fix adopted: probe scripts are written fresh per round, never sed-renamed. (3) The first hub tracing pass failed wholesale (300 TRACE-FAIL, empty ids): the trace script was composed through an SSH heredoc and arrived mangled. Rewritten as a local file, scp'd, re-run: 300/300 traced, all hashes matched. Runs: Run A preflight 753 s, run 87 s (1,218 matches/s run-phase - the fastest recorded), Run B preflight 438 s, run 108 s (981 matches/s); fleet 16/18 both runs (halycon-vector and rock-mountain preflight-excluded). Round totals: 216,380 matches screened (106,000 Run A + 106,000 Run B + 4,080 probe arms + 300 mechanism recordings).
Round 36 - Ranch Scale: the Band and the Window, Three Candidates in One Run (EE 822-826)
On Will's direction in chat: "iterate at ranch scale." The ranked hunks from the weakness register (scroll 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.37) that Round 35 left standing - W2 (deny rado's Hail band) and W3 (hit macro's flood in its Post window) - are built together: full fleet in parallel, full-depth tables, THREE candidates screened in one coordinated round, plus their combination. v22-hail is the parent; v16 stays seated; the submission hold stands. SCREEN-class evidence only: no registry transitions, nothing uploaded, nothing submitted, no xp-requests launched.

THE BUILDS - each ONE minimal diff from v22-hail, derived from the register's W2/W3 entries and v22's code (diffs incl. comments: v26 30 lines, v27 29, v28 59 = the verbatim union; deck, aim/swing/teamcalc otherwise verbatim; smoke-tested clean, 72/72 local matches, no player errors). (1) v26-band (bots/v26-band.bas), W2: in score, when the card being aimed is Shields (+0/+1, baseset-verified), our own minion is ranked by LOWEST current toughness first (value = 30 - hp*4 + power) instead of the generic help ranking - the most-damaged body is restored out of the 1-tough kill band first; and in swing, a non-killing chip that would leave an enemy body at exactly 1 toughness is devalued to 1 (never leave a remnant that feeds his band; Ranged bodies that take no combat damage are exempt). (2) v27-posthail (bots/v27-posthail.bas), W3: the card loop additionally counts foeOneTough (enemy bodies at current toughness 1) and postLive (any living opponent holds a Post trinket, boardName$ idiom); Hail's gate drops from >= 8 total enemy bodies to >= 5 with >= 3 of them 1-tough while postLive - the register's shape taken literally, on v22's foeMinions counting base. (3) v28-bandpost (bots/v28-bandpost.bas): both hunks, verbatim.

DECISION RULES, stated in analyze36.py's header before any tally existed: W2's mechanism moves iff (w2a) our 1-tough exposure at rado's Hail windows AND (w2b) his kills-per-fire on us both fall vs v22. W3's mechanism moves iff (w3a) our Hail kills-per-fire inside Post windows rises vs v22 AND neither macro's bodies/game (w3b) nor his stranded-energy loss-turn rate (w3c) rises. A candidate advances iff its mechanism moved AND its league-shaped share beats v22's same-round mark AND its gauntlet pooled value does not bleed. The combo advances only if it beats the better parent on the same terms. A hunk whose mechanism metric does not move is dead regardless of shares.

GATE 1 - ALL THREE SCREEN-BLIND. v26-band: 1 of 2,040 paired cells divergent (0.05%, zero missing). v27-posthail: 0 of 2,040 (0.00%). v28-bandpost: 0 of 2,040 (0.00%). Six probe nodes, fresh-written probe scripts (the Round 33/35 process fix held - no sed-renamed files), seed ranges 760000/761000/762000. The blindness is structural, and named as such: the probe table (candidate seat against v16, v11, v6, mage reference) seats NO Hail carrier and NO Post - the mechanisms' substrates do not exist in the gate's geometry, so the gate cannot see these hunks either way. Per the gate's own doctrine the claims route to the mechanism traces; per gauntlet rule 2, blind candidates carry no gauntlet headline value (their GC/GD tables were run in the fleet run and are recorded below as labeled, non-headline numbers).

MECHANISM - 900 traced league-shaped recordings this round (300 per candidate arm) read against v22's Round 34 recordings on the IDENTICAL seed plan (800000+m, R = m%5; rado-replica + macro-replica + warrior + archer): hashes matched everywhere (v22 45,274; v26 45,277; v27 45,274; v28 45,277). W2: rado-replica fires Hail 350 times (1.17/game) in every arm. (w2a) our 1-tough exposure at his fire moments: 0.466 bodies per fire, total 163 - IDENTICAL in v26 and v22. (w2b) his kills-per-fire on us: 0.466, total 163 - identical (kills equal exposure by construction: Hail deals exactly 1, so every exposed body dies; the metric that had to move was exposure, and it did not move at all). The hunk demonstrably fires - v26's games diverge from v22's (hash totals differ; its own outside-window Hail count moves 58 -> 59) - but the flow it dams is too thin: our Warrior board presents under half a 1-tough body per fire window to begin with, combat leaves few, and four Shields copies aimed at play-time cannot pre-position against windows rado chooses. W2's mechanism DOES NOT MOVE; per the stated rule the hunk is dead regardless of shares. W3: our Hail fires inside Post windows - 12 in v27, 12 in v22, with identical kills/fire (3.583) on what are, in aggregate, the same games (v27's hash total equals v22's exactly; every macro metric identical). THE DROPPED GATE OPENED ZERO ADDITIONAL FIRES IN 300 GAMES. The window itself is real and rich - v22's own in-window kills/fire read 3.583 against 2.724 outside - but the gate as specified counts the four-opponent total (v22's foeMinions, kept verbatim), and in Post windows that total is already >= 8 whenever the window's own conditions (>= 5 bodies, >= 3 of them 1-tough) hold: the standing gate dominates the dropped one everywhere it was measured. W3's mechanism DOES NOT MOVE. (w3b)/(w3c), identical across arms because the games are: macro bodies/game 22.18; stranded loss-turn rate 33.2% (678/2,045 - the replica's read against the audit's hosted 30.8%). COMBO: v28's traced read is v26's exactly - it inherits a flat W2 and an inert W3 and beats neither parent; there is no better parent to beat.

GATE 2 - ONE combined fleet run (17 tables, 21,200 matches each, 360,400 total, seed plan 3700000:4240, fleet 16/18, 663 chunks, zero retries): LEAGUE-SHAPED (headline): L22 v22 6.4% (1,360), L26 v26 6.4% (1,363), L27 v27 6.4% (1,357), L28 v28 6.4% (1,360) - parity to the tenth of a point at ranch depth; the replicas' shares are unmoved (rado 60.4, macro 15.6 in every L table). Table CF, seventh reproduction of the post-refresh field: rado-replica 43.7, v11 20.4, v16 15.4, v17-value 10.5, macro-replica 10.2. CF in the CF3 composition (candidate in the v11 seat): v26 20.1, v27 20.2, v28 20.1 - inside the standing band (v22 20.0 R33, v25 19.5 R35). GAUNTLET: Table G re-measured 62.3 / 13.9 / 13.5 / 7.7 / 2.6 - counts identical to Round 35's Run B because this run's gauntlet tables share that run's seed plan (3700000): a same-plan determinism reproduction, claimed as exactly that and no more. v22's subject pooled value, quotable: 10.2% (GC 9.2, GD 11.1). The candidates' pooled GC/GD reads (v26 10.2, v27 10.2, v28 10.2) are recorded here as labeled non-headline values per gauntlet rule 2 - no bleed in any case. Seed-plan note: this run's L/CF tables are on a fresh plan against Round 35's Run A (3600000), so those comparisons are cross-plan; the gauntlet comparisons are same-plan.

VERDICT: no candidate advances - both mechanisms flat under their stated decision rules, shares at parity everywhere, combo dominated by its own parents' flatness. v22-hail remains the advancing line and the next build's parent; v16 stays seated; the submission hold stands on unchanged evidence. DISTANCE TO THE BAR: league-shaped best 6.4% against the #1's league mean_score 0.327 (EE 709) - about 26 points, the fourth straight round in the 6.4-6.6 band. MOAT: no transitions (True 14, False 7, Unknown 15, Fiction 2) - all evidence SCREEN-class. WHAT SURVIVES: (1) The falsification taxonomy grows: Round 34's mechanism fired and was priced out by the life term; Round 35's fired and was overdetermined by the field's fire; Round 36's W2 fires against a flow too thin to dam, and W3 never fires because the standing gate dominates it. Four distinct failure shapes, each measured at the mechanism before shares were read. (2) W3's one live descendant, named not built: a Hail gate keyed to the POST-HOLDER'S board alone (>= 5 bodies with >= 3 1-tough on that board while its Post is live) - the four-opponent total is what made this round's gate inert, and the in-window kills/fire premium (3.583 vs 2.724) is measured support for the window's value if a gate can be made to bind. (3) W2's boundary is now measured, not guessed: at 0.466 exposed bodies per fire, band-denial via Shields is worth at most ~0.47 bodies per rado fire in this field - any future W2 shape must act on the exposure flow itself (combat outcomes), not on buff targeting.

MACHINERY AND INCIDENTS, named: all fleet work ran from the hash-pinned snapshot (cac-dist/r36/, round.sh sha256 05f3d8c1, unchanged since Round 32). The single combined run: preflight 986 s (ABOC compile path OK; fleet 16/18 - halycon-vector and rock-mountain preflight-excluded), run phase 279 s = 1,292 matches/s, the fastest recorded, 663/663 chunks complete on attempt 0. Probes: 3 x 2,040 cells over 6 nodes, zero missing (kaleidoscope-one's v28 shard ran ~2 minutes longer than its peers, inside its timeout). Recordings ran on the local v3 build and were traced on the hub (900/900, zero TRACE-FAIL). Incidents: (1) analyze36.py's first pass keyed card plays to action kind 3 (plays are kind 1; kind 2 is attack, kind 3 setup) and read zero Hail fires in EVERY arm including the v22 control - a metric that reads zero on its control arm is an instrument error, not a result; the definition was corrected in the analyzer's header and code before any verdict was drawn, and the kind-independent macro metrics were unaffected. (2) The trace pull-back tarball exited 2 on ownership restoration (hub uid 1000 vs local) - contents verified complete by count (900/900) before analysis; the exit code short-circuited the chained first analyzer run, which was then run directly. (3) Preflight remains the pipeline's largest block (986 s of the run's 1,265 s) - serial session establishment through the shared egress proxy, contention-dominated; the named lever (cross-run master persistence) stands. The progress chart (cac-dist/progress-chart.html) is extended through Round 36. Round totals: 360,400 matches screened + 6,120 paired probe cells + 900 traced recordings.
Round 37 - The Mage Line: Two Coherent Mage Builds; One Reproduces the Flood (EE 836-840)
On Will's direction in chat: "iterate with the mage." Rounds 30-36 falsified seven consecutive single-mechanism transfers on the Warrior shell, four rounds flat at ~26 points to the bar. The Mage line was the untouched lever: macromackie's Mage draw is the corpus's largest number (0.403 over 236 hosted games, against his Warrior draw's 0.284 - register W7), and our own Mage attempts were all pre-instrument: v8-mage scored 0 of 40 hosted, v10-mage-long a dead heat against Mage stock, v13 collapsed on a misread Burnout - all judged against stock fields, before the replicas, before the gauntlet. This round retests the Mage line properly: two coherent builds (not hunks), mechanism metrics first, Gate 2 on the refreshed floors, v22 and v16 as same-round baselines. v16 stays seated; the submission hold stands. SCREEN-class evidence only: nothing uploaded, nothing submitted, no xp-requests launched.

THE BUILDS. v29-magepure: Mage hero, the STOCK Mage deck verbatim (Bouncer, Spirit, Plan, Study, Summon Primordial, Bubble Shield, Oozification, Morphosis Chamber, Overwork, Control, x4 each), our line's logic chassis (v22's aim/score/swing/teamcalc) adapted - a two-pass play loop (engine pass: Overwork/Plan/Study/Bubble Shield/Morphosis Chamber; then bodies and removal) and Mage keep-values in the toss (the engine and the finishers are never tossed). Not macro cosplay: the pure shell has no Post and no shooters; its claim is the draw engine. v30-magehybrid: Mage hero, macromackie's C2 shell verbatim (Archer x12, Bubble, Sniper, Overwork, Plan, Post, Sharpshooter, Study, x4 each) with his measured disciplines implemented as rules on OUR logic: Bubble on sight; Archer trinkets next (the discount engine - each Archer in play cuts the Archer-card surcharge by 1); Post only with a minion in hand; Overwork; minions held for a live Post (hand-overflow release at 7); draw spells after development; Sharpshooter pings aimed at the lowest-life enemy hero and never at a creature, enforced at the score level; discards on his measured keep table (toss redundancy, never a Sharpshooter/Post/Overwork). Attacks and focus remain our line's (v22 swing, highest-life outsider focus) - a stated divergence from his lowest-life race, kept deliberately: the candidate differs from macro-replica by its logic, not by its costume, or the comparison means nothing. TEAM PROTOCOL: does not apply to either build, decided from the format - the league seats ONE policy, so both carry teamcalc in its league form (partner forced to -1, the Round 32 lesson: partner arithmetic in solo fields protects strangers); the paired-seat protocol remains a Warrior-family test-roster artifact. Baseset read before designing around any card (the v13 rule): Post (1, lasts 2) copies a played Archer minion of cost <= 3 and gives it Ready; Bubble is a 0-cost Mage trinket that bounces the first attacker and dies; Overwork (3, lasts 3) gives +3 energy on play and +2/draw 1 per turn, and summons Burnout when destroyed - carried knowingly, as macro carries it (register W4: aboard in 54% of his wins).

GATE 1 (Divergence Gate): v29-magepure 67.01% (1,367 of 2,040 paired cells divergent vs v22), v30-magehybrid 69.71% (1,422 of 2,040), zero missing - the widest divergences the gate has recorded, as class + deck changes should read. Both SIGHTED; both earn gauntlet headlines.

MECHANISM (decision rules fixed in analyze37.py's header before any tally; 300 recorded league-shaped matches per arm on the identical seed plan 800000+, traces hash-validated: v22 45,274, v29 48,538, v30 44,393 - every hash matched). v30 SHAPE: MATCH, all five clauses. Bodies/game 20.10 against macro-replica's Mage-family 23.30 in the same rooms (the bar was 0.75x = 17.47); minion plays 3.07/game; Post-copy conversion 6.55 bodies per minion play against the replica's 6.67 (bar 5.01); draws 15.3/game; stranded loss-turn rate 27.2% against the replica-Mage's 32.0% (bar: replica + 5); Post played with a minion in hand 100%; minion plays under a live Post 98.4%; Sharpshooter pings 482 hero / 0 creature / 0 other. Death profile: mean placement 3.03 against the v22 arm's 4.31, first-out rate 28.3% against 62.7%, recorded win share 17.7% against the v22 arm's 7.3% on the same plan. The flood's shape - bodies from copies rather than plays, energy spent rather than stranded, shooters pinging heroes - is reproduced by our logic on his shell: the first mechanism of the post-refresh era to match its target shape. v29 SHAPE: PASS on its own stated test (draws 16.0/game against the 1.25x bar on v22's 6.0 = 7.4; bodies 13.41 against v22's 7.92) - and the shape does not convert: recorded win share 3.7%, placement 3.88, first-out 36.3%. The pure Mage draws and fields (its 13.41 bodies come from only 2.13 minion plays - Bubble Shield, Oozification and Summon Primordial summons), but the bodies are 1/1s and bounce tricks against corpus-strength fields: draw without teeth. Suppression read (the replica in our rooms): macro-replica's all-combo win share is 27.7% in v29's rooms, 20.3% in v30's, 19.0% in v22's; his Mage-family bodies/game run 27.64 in v29's rooms against 23.30 in v30's - the hybrid contests his board space; the pure line feeds it.

GATE 2 (one fleet run, 15 tables x 21,200 = 318,000 matches, seed plan 3800000:4240, fleet 16/18). LEAGUE-SHAPED (headline): L30 v30 20.3% (4,314) - triple v22's same-round L22 mark of 6.6% (1,390); L16 v16 6.1% (1,296); L29 v29 3.3% (698). In L30 the rado-replica falls to 51.1% (from 60.5% in L22) while macro-replica holds 15.6%: v30 is the second seat in the league-shaped room. A reading, labeled as such: rado's scored rule (life - 2*boardPower + boardCount) prices the widest board last - register W1's geometry - and the flood rebuilds through his Hail band faster than his focus dismantles it; the spared-executioner shape works for the flood instead of against it. CF3 COMPOSITION (subject in the v11 seat): CF30 v30 21.7%, the best lineage mark in that composition (CF22 v22 20.0% same round; CF29 v29 8.0%). Table CF, eighth reproduction of the post-refresh field: rado-replica 43.8, v11 20.5, v16 15.4, v17-value 10.6, macro-replica 9.7. GAUNTLET (cost side): Table G re-measured 62.8 / 13.5 / 13.1 / 7.8 / 2.8. Subject pooled: v22 9.8% (GC 8.8, GD 10.8); v29 1.3% (GC 1.3, GD 1.2); v30 2.4% (GC 2.3, GD 2.5) - both Mage values quotable, both heavily bled.

VERDICT under the advance rule stated before the tallies (shape test passed AND league-shaped share above v22's same-round mark AND gauntlet pooled bleed no more than 1 point against v22's same-round pooled value): v29-magepure fails on shares (3.3% against 6.6%, gauntlet 1.3%) - the pure Mage line is closed on this evidence; the stock shell plus our logic is not a line. v30-magehybrid passes the shape test and the headline by the largest margins the programme has recorded - and fails the gauntlet clause by 7.4 points (2.4% against 9.8%, allowance 1). THE RULE BINDS: v30 does not advance; v22-hail remains the advancing line and the next build's parent; v16 stays seated; the submission hold stands. What the scroll must also name is what the gauntlet measured: Tables GC/GD seat v11 + v16 + v17-value - three Warrior-line bots carrying twelve Hail of Arrows between them - plus one stock reference, against a Mage board printed at toughness 1. That is our own line's monoculture; the league never seats it (league-shaped fields are the two replicas plus references, where v30 triples the line's mark and takes 9.4 points off the rado floor). Whether the gauntlet thereby prices cross-class candidates, or merely prices Hail against 1-toughness bodies, is a question about the instrument - and gauntlet.txt fixes the tables and provides that changing them starts a new gauntlet version, inscribed as such; it is not this round's to change unilaterally. THE DECISION NAMED FOR WILL: (a) hold the rule as stated - v30 stays a challenger and the Warrior line keeps the title outright; (b) charter Gauntlet v2 with a cross-class subject composition for class-changing candidates (v1 retained for same-class hunks); (c) re-scope the advance rule so the gauntlet clause binds only within-class candidates, with cross-class advances judged on shape + league-shaped + CF surfaces. Until Will rules, the formal state is unchanged. DISTANCE TO THE BAR: the league-shaped best is now 20.3% against the #1's league mean_score 0.327 (EE 709) - about 12 points, the first movement in five rounds (Rounds 33-36 held at ~26). MOAT: no registry transitions - all Round 37 evidence is SCREEN-class; counts unchanged (True 14, False 7, Unknown 15, Fiction 2).

MACHINERY AND INCIDENTS, named: all fleet work ran from the hash-pinned snapshot (cac-dist/r37/, round.sh sha256 05f3d8c1, unchanged since Round 32). The single run: preflight 487 s (ABOC compile path OK, 16 icecc daemons), run phase 181 s = 1,757 matches/s, the fastest recorded; 585 chunks; fleet 16/18 (halycon-vector and rock-mountain preflight-excluded, the standing pair). Probes: 2 x 2,040 cells over 6 nodes, zero missing after top-ups. Recordings traced on the hub: 900/900, zero TRACE-FAIL. Incidents: (1) The first probe wave launched both candidates' dispatches concurrently per node; the shards share per-node jobs/results filenames, so returned files pooled both candidates' cells - recovered exactly by content-keyed dedupe (each cell names its candidate) plus sequential top-up shards for the missing seed ranges; ashfall-haven's first shards returned empty under the same race and were re-dispatched cleanly. Both candidates closed at exactly 2,040 cells, zero missing. Process fix, inscribed: probe dispatches for different candidates run SEQUENTIALLY per node, always. (2) analyze37.py's first ping metric keyed on a DamageEvent cause field that this trace format leaves empty (the DamageEvent's card is the victim's); it read zero pings in every arm INCLUDING macro-replica, whose corpus discipline is 1,052 hero pings and 0 creature pings - a control-arm zero is an instrument error, not a result (the Round 36 rule). Corrected to the PlayEvent target keying and verified by hand on traced Sharpshooter plays (subject, replica and reference seats) before any verdict was drawn; the corrected control reads 411-570 pings per room, all heroes, matching the corpus. All other metrics are kind- and board-based and were unaffected. (3) A VM-side wait poll returned an empty body mid-round (output drain); the run's own timing.txt is the record (preflight 487 s, total 668 s) and no work was lost or repeated. The progress chart (cac-dist/progress-chart.html) is extended through Round 37 (Panel 1 CF column at R37; gauntlet bars for v29/v30; the machinery axis rescaled to 1,800 to hold the 1,757 bar; notes and series table updated). Round totals: 318,000 matches screened + 4,080 paired probe cells + 900 traced recordings.
Amendment - The Advance Rule Re-Scoped: Will's Ruling (Option (c)); Round 37 Verdict Re-Issued (EE 842)
On 2026-11-26 at 02:17 CST, Will ruled on the decision named for him in scroll 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.41. His words: "Re-scope the rule — gauntlet clause binds only within-class candidates" - option (c) of the three that scroll named ((a) hold the rule as stated; (b) charter Gauntlet v2 with a cross-class subject composition; (c) re-scope the clause). This scroll is the record of that ruling: the amended rule, the verdict it re-issues, and what does not change. It is an amendment, not a round - no matches were screened, no candidate was built, nothing was uploaded, nothing was submitted, no xp-requests were launched. All evidence cited is Round 37's, SCREEN-class; MOAT: no transitions (True 14, False 7, Unknown 15, Fiction 2).

THE AMENDED RULE (canonical text now carried in gauntlet.txt, "THE ADVANCE RULE"; the analyzer headers of Rounds 36 and 37 carry post-round amendment notes, their pre-tally texts standing as stated). The advance rule stands as the programme has run it since Round 28: a candidate becomes the advancing line iff its mechanism/shape test passed AND its league-shaped share beats the advancing line's same-round league-shaped mark AND its gauntlet pooled subject value does not bleed beyond the round's stated allowance against the advancing line's same-round pooled value (Round 37 allowance: 1 point); a candidate whose share wins but whose shape test fails is an unexplained residual, not an advance (Round 34 doctrine). THE AMENDMENT, in scope only: the gauntlet no-bleed clause binds ONLY within-class candidates - a candidate in the same hero class as the advancing line it challenges. A cross-class candidate is judged on its mechanism/shape test, its league-shaped share, and the CF / CF3 compositions. Its gauntlet pooled value is still measured every round, still recorded, and still priced in the round's scroll as the cost side - never hidden - but it does not block the advance.

WHAT DOES NOT CHANGE. Gauntlet v1 is not amended and no new version is chartered: Table G stays fixed forever (v11, v16, v17-value, warrior, archer), Tables GC / GD keep their compositions, and the headline discipline stands (headline values only from G / GC / GD; baselines re-measured, never carried). The Divergence Gate is untouched. v16 stays seated in the league. The submission hold stands, and Will's criterion stands with it - "we'll submit when we have a shot at winning": advancement under this rule is a local line decision, not a submission, and the bar is unmet (below).

VERDICT RE-ISSUED. Under the amended rule, Round 37's verdict re-issues: v30-magehybrid ADVANCES. It is a cross-class candidate (Mage hero against the Warrior line); its shape test matched macromackie's flood on all five stated clauses (bodies/game 20.10 against the replica-Mage's 23.30 in the same rooms; Post-copy conversion 6.55 against 6.67; Post-with-minion 100%; minion plays under a live Post 98.4%; Sharpshooter pings 482 hero / 0 creature; stranded rate 27.2% against the replica's 32.0%); its league-shaped share was 20.3% against v22's same-round 6.6%; its CF3-composition mark was 21.7%, the best lineage mark in that composition. Its gauntlet pooled value - 2.4% against v22's 9.8%, a 7.4-point bleed on the Warrior-monoculture tables - remains measured, recorded, and priced as its cost side; under the amended rule it does not block a cross-class advance. v30-magehybrid is the advancing line and the next build's parent. v22-hail is recorded as the Warrior-line best, and its gauntlet standing remains the within-class bar: any future Warrior candidate must clear the no-bleed clause in full, as v23, v24, v25, v26, v27 and v28 were bound by it (all within-class; no earlier verdict changes under this amendment - Rounds 30-36 re-read under the amended rule return the same verdicts, because every candidate before Round 37 challenged within its own class). v29-magepure stays closed (it failed on shares under any reading of the rule). DISTANCE TO THE BAR: the advancing line's league-shaped mark is 20.3% against the #1 contender's league mean_score 0.327 (EE 709) - about 12 points short, the first movement in five rounds (Rounds 33-36 held at ~26). The bar is not reached; the hold stands on Will's criterion, unchanged by this ruling.

RECORD OF THE AMENDMENT. Amended by Will's ruling, 2026-11-26, option (c): gauntlet.txt (advance rule stated canonically with the scope amendment; the fixed DEFINITION untouched); cac-dist/top2/analyze37.py and analyze36.py headers (amendment notes appended; pre-tally rule texts preserved verbatim); cac-dist/top2/state.md (advancing line = v30-magehybrid; v22-hail = Warrior-line best / within-class gauntlet bar; ruling addendum appended; the Round 37 addendum's verdict line marked superseded); cac-dist/make_progress_chart.py and the regenerated progress-chart.html (Round 37 narrative and series table carry the ruling; v30 marked as the advancing line from R37). This scroll is the phext record. No Round 38 is opened by this amendment - the next build is a separate direction.
Round 38 - The Clock, Both Directions: Capping Our Burnout and Discounting His (EE 844-846)
The first round built on the Mage line under Will's ruling (option (c), scroll 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.42): v30-magehybrid is the advancing line and this round's parent, and both candidates are WITHIN-CLASS (Mage against Mage), so the gauntlet no-bleed clause binds in full at the stated 1-point allowance. The round opened with a loss autopsy of the parent, and both hunks were named by it. VERDICT IN BRIEF: no candidate advances - v31-clock starves the engine it was meant to protect (its premise, that our Burnout deaths are stack-driven, is falsified by its own mechanism metrics), and v32-burndiscount does exactly what it was built to do at zero measured cost and lands at parity with its parent (league-shaped 20.4% against 20.4%), which under the rule is not a beat. v30-magehybrid remains the advancing line and the next build's parent; v16 stays seated; the submission hold stands. All evidence is SCREEN-class; MOAT: no transitions (True 14, False 7, Unknown 15, Fiction 2).

THE AUTOPSY (autopsy38.py, corrected by autopsy38b.py, on Round 37's traced v30 arm - 300 league-shaped games, identical seed plan; pass 1's death detection missed deaths on a game's final action and is superseded by pass 2, which keys on the DefeatEvent). v30 won 53 and lost 247. Winners of the lost games: rado-replica 149, macro-replica 61, warrior 30, archer 7 - rado mostly OUTLIVES us rather than killing us. Killers: macro-replica 112 (his flood's bodies - Sharpshooter and Sniper attacks), rado 75 (and at our death against rado we are his scored rule's argmin in only 19 of 75; rank 2 in 56 - he reaches us second), OUR OWN BURNOUT 30 (12.1% of all losses), warrior 21, archer 9. Placements in losses: first out 85, then 62, 41, and 59 second-place finishes. Death state: a wide, weak board (8.82 bodies, 4.35 power), 4.31 energy unspent, hand of 1.86 cards - and the payload still in it: a Sharpshooter sat unplayed in 118 losses (183 copies), a Sniper in 110; a Post in only 9. The bodies gap against replica-Mage (20.10 against 23.30) decomposes as SURVIVAL, not sequencing: every card plays less often per game for v30, but per-own-turn rates are at parity (draws per turn 2.26 against 2.37; Post plays per turn 0.279 against 0.286; Post uptime 39.4% against 40.6%; conversion 6.55 against 6.67) - macro-Mage simply lives 7.8 own turns per game to our 6.8. The baseset was read before designing (the Burnout lesson): Overwork lasts 3 turns, pays extra energy and draw while alive, and ON DESTROYED summons a Burnout - 2 damage and a forced toss at each of its owner's end-of-turns, with no expiry, and Burnouts STACK (control trace m0: macro died at life 3 to two simultaneous Burnout triggers). v30 plays 1.91 Overworks a game: it restarts and stacks its own clock. The tax is symmetric and heavier on the champion: macro-Mage died to his own clock in 51 of his 173 losses in the same rooms (29.5%).

THE BUILDS (each one minimal diff from v30; make38bots.py; smoke-tested clean). v31-clock: a board scan for a running clock (an Overwork or a Burnout of ours aboard); once one exists, no further Overwork is played and spare Overworks become toss redundancy (keep 95 -> 0). Everything else verbatim v30. v32-burndiscount (weakness register W4): a burnscan of any hero's board; hero damage - minion swings, card damage, Sharpshooter pings - into a BURNING enemy hero at life <= 4 scores 0 when it would not kill this action; lethal damage keeps full value. Everything else verbatim v30.

GATE 1 (divergence, paired cells against the parent, 2,040 cells each, zero missing; dispatches sequential per candidate - the Round 37 race did not recur): v31 33.38% SIGHTED (the cap rewrites the Overwork economy, and everything downstream moves); v32 2.70% SIGHTED (the W4 band is rare but real). Both candidates' gauntlet values are quotable.

MECHANISM (300 traced games per arm, identical seed plan; control is Round 37's v30 arm re-used - hashes 44,393/44,393 already verified; v31 44,483/44,483 and v32 44,466/44,466 matched, zero TRACE-FAIL). v31: the cap BINDS - Overwork 0.91 plays/game against the parent's 1.91, games with >= 2 Burnouts 0 against 108, stacking eliminated. And the deaths do not move: self-Burnout deaths 29 against the parent's 30. The premise dies here - our clock deaths are SINGLE-clock deaths; one permanent Burnout is the whole lethality, and the second clock was never our problem. The cost is real and priced: draws/game 13.8 against 15.3, minion plays 2.63 against 3.07, bodies/game 16.95 against the shape bar of 18.09 (0.75x the in-room replica-Mage's 24.12) - SHAPE FAILS, and the recorded win share falls to 12.0% against 17.7%. v32: the discount BINDS - W4-band waste (non-lethal damage events into burning heroes at life <= 4) falls from the parent's 18 events (0.060/game) to ZERO. Shape kept in substance: bodies 20.14 against the 17.53 bar, conversion 6.57, stranded 27.5%, Post-with-minion 100%, pings 480 hero / 0 creature / 2 other - the 2 "other" identified by hand as DECLINES in game m298, a heads-up endgame against a burning hero at life 3, i.e. the hunk declining exactly where it was built to decline (the analyzer's shape clause counted declines as non-hero pings; the corpus discipline it guards - never a creature, 1,052/0 - is intact; the clause's wording is corrected in analyze38.py's post-round note). macro's own clock deaths in-room are unmoved (52 against the parent's 51): the band is real, our waste in it was small, and removing the waste does not hasten his clock.

GATE 2 (one fleet run, 15 tables x 21,200 = 318,000 matches, fresh seed plan 3900000:4240). League-shaped: L30 v30 20.4% (4,321), L31 v31 15.1% (3,204), L32 v32 20.4% (4,326), L22 v22 6.6% (the Warrior-line reference, stable). v32's margin over its parent is 5 matches in 21,200 - parity by every convention this programme has used (Round 33 called 6.5 against 6.4 parity at ten times that gap). CF3 composition: CF30 v30 21.5% (4,548), CF31 v31 16.9% (3,580), CF32 v32 21.6% (4,578). Table CF, ninth reproduction: rado-replica 44.2, v11 20.4, v16 15.1, v17-value 10.6, macro-replica 9.7. Table G reproduced (v17-value 62.4, v11 13.7, v16 13.7, warrior 7.7, archer 2.5). GAUNTLET, the clause binding (within-class): pooled v30 2.42% (477 + 547), v31 1.85% (389 + 395 - a 0.57 bleed, inside the 1-point allowance, and moot given its shares), v32 2.42% (477 + 547 - its GC and GD counts are its parent's EXACTLY, because no gauntlet seat carries Overwork: the W4 band has no substrate in the gauntlet field, so the clause passes v32 by construction, and this scroll names that so no future round mistakes it for league-field evidence - v32 was priced in L and CF, at parity).

VERDICT under the advance rule as amended (mechanism moved AND league-shaped beats the parent's same-round mark AND, within-class, the gauntlet clause passes): v31-clock fails the mechanism's substance (deaths 29 against 30), fails the shape, and fails the headline by 5.3 points - CLOSED; the Overwork cap is not a line, and the diagnosis it produced (single-clock lethality) replaces the one it was built on. v32-burndiscount passes its mechanism cleanly and passes the gauntlet clause, and fails the headline by the only margin that matters - there is none: 20.4% against 20.4% is parity, not a beat. It does NOT advance. It is recorded as a verified, zero-cost component: the waste it removes is real (18 events a round at this depth, every one of them damage the parent spends on a hero the clock already owns), and a future combined build may carry it without paying for it anywhere this round could measure. DISTANCE TO THE BAR: league-shaped best 20.4% against the #1's league mean_score 0.327 (EE 709) - about 12 points, the second consecutive round at ~12 (Round 37 moved it from ~26; this round holds it). v30-magehybrid remains the advancing line and the next build's parent; v16 stays seated; the submission hold stands on Will's criterion.

WHAT SURVIVES: (1) The corrected clock diagnosis: our Burnout deaths are single-clock - the lethality is one permanent 2-and-a-toss per turn arriving the moment the first Overwork expires, and it is the engine's price, paid by the champion at more than twice our rate (29.5% of his losses). Future clock work, if any, must address the single clock's endgame (life management while it ticks), not its stacking - or accept the price as the cost of the draw engine, as macro's line demonstrably does. (2) The W4 discount as a banked component: mechanism verified at the trace, cost zero on every surface measured (league-shaped, CF3, gauntlet, shape), benefit capped locally by the band's rarity - it is the first hunk since the Hail package to be kept on evidence of harmlessness plus a measured mechanism, rather than on a share. (3) A named instrument boundary: clock mechanics are gauntlet-invisible (no seat carries Overwork), so within-class clock hunks will always pass the gauntlet clause by construction; their price must be read in L/CF - where this round read it.

MACHINERY AND INCIDENTS, named: all fleet work ran from the hash-pinned snapshot (cac-dist/r38/, round.sh sha256 05f3d8c1 and cac-round 13545c71, unchanged since Round 32). The run: preflight 513 s (ABOC compile path OK), run phase 195 s = 1,631 matches/s (second fastest recorded; Round 37's 1,757 stands), 586 chunks, fleet 16/18 (halycon-vector and rock-mountain preflight-excluded, the standing pair), total 708 s. Probes: 2 x 2,040 cells over 6 nodes, sequential per candidate, zero missing, no top-ups needed. Recordings: 600 new matches traced on the hub, 600/600, zero TRACE-FAIL; the v30 control arm is Round 37's recordings on the identical seed plan (the Round 36 precedent). Incidents: (1) The autopsy's first pass missed every death on a game's final action (59 of 247 losses, mostly second-place finishes) because it required a next action's pre-state; caught when the winner and killer tables failed to reconcile, corrected in pass 2 by keying on the DefeatEvent, and pass 1's killer table is superseded wherever the two differ. (2) The trace pull-back tarball exited 2 on ownership restoration (hub uid 1000 against local) - the Round 36 incident recurring; contents verified complete by count (300 + 300) before analysis. (3) analyze38.py's shape clause read v32's two in-band ping declines as discipline failures; identified by hand-trace (m298) as the hunk's intended behavior and corrected as an instrument wording error in the analyzer's post-round note - the pre-tally decision rules stand as stated, and the correction is recorded rather than silently applied. The progress chart (cac-dist/progress-chart.html) is extended through Round 38 (Panel 1 CF column at R38; CF3, league-shaped and gauntlet bars for v31/v32; machinery bars at 1,631 matches/s; notes and series table updated). Round totals: 318,000 matches screened + 4,080 paired probe cells + 600 traced recordings.
Champion Succession - v30-magehybrid Seated: Will's Word, "submit" (EE 846)
On 2026-11-26 at 02:44 CST, Will directed, in chat: "submit." The standing gate on this programme - league submissions, policy uploads for submission, and hosted xp-requests only on Will's word in chat - is satisfied by that direction. The submission criterion Will set on 2026-11-24 ("we'll submit when we have a shot at winning") is his to judge; the evidence on the table at his word was Round 37's and Round 38's: v30-magehybrid the advancing line under the amended advance rule (scrolls .41-.43), league-shaped 20.3-20.4% against the Warrior line's 6.6%, distance about 12 points to the #1 contender's league mean. The criterion was not re-litigated; the direction was executed. This scroll is the record: pre-state, upload, submission, succession, post-state - every id verified against live platform state before and after, not carried from memory.

PRE-STATE (live pull, 2026-11-26T08:45Z, EE 846). Seated champion: emise-cac-v16:v1 - membership lpm_06a22376-798a-40b3-b76d-04687ba3e0de, policy version adae4ee8-c75c-40ed-9585-2a6963bac8fa, submission sub_8d445f15-fe7f-4604-a601-2788c3eebdd6, status competing / active, is_champion true, seated since 2026-11-24T08:12:52Z. emise-cac-v6:v1 benched (membership lpm_2c66caea-7315-4731-9cbe-dff3d12005b7, version 248f926f-e402-4aee-a52e-97802070cac5). Division standings at the pull: player-61986354 (ply_946b4a58-772c-4a44-8cb9-9d8918c70236) stood #7 of 9 - MMR 18.171, mean_score 0.152, 221 rounds played, all of them v16's. The top of the board: #1 Andre von Auto, MMR 26.647, mean 0.345; #2 macromackie, MMR 25.606, mean 0.329 - the top-2 order flipped against the EE 709 pull (then macromackie #1 at 0.327, Andre #2 at 0.343); recorded here as observed, at submission time.

