Round 39 - The Combo and the Release: Banked Parts, Deployed Payloads, and the First Hosted Read (EE 879-892)

THE ORDER. At EE 879 (2026-11-26 07:34 CST) Will directed: "accelerate study and iteration, train continuously within thermal limits." This round is the order's first execution: a thermal protocol established from measurement and governing the round's machinery, the next iteration from Round 38's evidence, the first study of our own seated champion's hosted episodes, and a continuous-training loop created to keep the programme running between directions (its charter is the order itself; its hard limits are recorded under THE LOOP below).

THE THERMAL PROTOCOL (full text: ~/workspace/cac-dist/thermal-protocol.md; probe tool thermal-probe.sh; raw readings in thermal/). Measured baseline at EE 879: the 14 sensored ranch nodes idle at Tctl 30.8-41.9 C; aletheia-core, the working hub, idles hot at 63.6 C under its standing services; neon (WSL2 on lilly) exposes NO temperature sensors at all; halycon-vector and rock-mountain were SSH-unreachable (the standing excluded pair). Under load the hub at slots 4 read Tctl 86.8 C - the fleet's hot node by a wide margin, and the protocol's formative measurement. The ladder: pre-probe < 55 C runs slots 8; 55-70 slots 4; 70-80 slots 2 (hot set only); >= 80 excluded; under load, >= 85 C on two consecutive probes reassigns the node's chunks, >= 90 C stops it at once; sensorless nodes are capped at slots 4 permanently; cooldown: no node starts a new round at >= 55 C (the hub, >= 60 C). Mechanization: a round runs as two round.sh invocations over disjoint seed-range halves of one plan - cool set at slots 8, hot set at slots 4 - tallies summed. This round ran exactly that split.

THE CANDIDATES. Round 38 banked v32-burndiscount (the W4 discount: verified mechanism, zero measured cost, parity shares) and the autopsy named the survival direction: the bodies gap is survival, and we die holding payload - Sharpshooter unplayed in 118 of 247 traced losses, Sniper in 110, 4.31 energy unspent at death - because v30's flood discipline freezes every minion while no Post is live and the hand is under 7. The hunk chosen from the autopsy's three candidates is PAYLOAD DEPLOYMENT (the release): the Post-hold lifts at playerLife(self) <= 8, the danger band where Round 35 measured death-once-lowest at ~95% and where W1/W4 already live. Endgame life-while-ticking was not chosen: Round 38 corrected that diagnosis to a survival problem (single-clock deaths), and the release attacks survival directly; closing-focus was not chosen: it is a pricing change on the Warrior-line pattern, and the Mage line's losses are not focus losses (rado outlives us because we die at turn ~29.5 with cards in hand, not because we aim wrong). Two arms, one-line diffs each, byte-verified against their parents (make39bots.py): v33-combined = v32 + the release; v34-release = v30 + the release alone (the ablation, so the combo's legs price separately).

GATE 1. Fresh probe scripts (node-probe39.sh, dispatch-probe39.sh), parents v32 and v30 respectively, 2,040 paired cells each: v33-combined diverges 6.81% (139/2040), v34-release 6.47% (132/2040) - both SIGHTED, zero missing cells. The release is a structural diff the screen can see.

MECHANISM (analyze39.py; rules in its header before tallies; 300 traced league-shaped games per arm on the identical seed plan; controls = Round 37's v30 arm and Round 38's v32 arm, hashes 44,291-44,466 per arm all matched). The analyzer first re-derives the autopsy on the v30 control: band plays 3, Sharpshooter-held deaths 118 of 247 losses (47.8%) - the instrument reproduces the finding it tests. The release BINDS in both candidates: band plays 174 (v33) / 172 (v34) across ~127 band games; Sharpshooter-held deaths fall to 74 (30.3% / 30.2% of losses); any-payload deaths 62.3% -> 48.4% / 48.2%. Minion plays per game rise 3.07 -> 3.56; bodies/game 20.10 -> 20.34 / 20.30. SHAPE KEPT on every Round 37 clause in both arms: Post-with-minion 100%, pings never a creature (559 hero / 0 creature in both; v33 shows 3 declines, read per Round 38's correction), bodies >= 0.75x the replica-Mage in-room, conversion 5.71 vs the replica's 6.67 (0.86x), stranded 25.2% / 24.9% vs the replica's ~32%. Survival read: traced win share 18.7% (v33) / 18.3% (v34) vs the control's 17.7%; placement and death turn unmoved (3.03, turn 29.5) - the release converts held payload into board and wins at the margin; it does not yet make us live longer, and the scroll says so plainly. v33's W4 leg is kept: waste 0 events (control 18), self-Burnout deaths 31 vs 30 (single-clock, Round 38's diagnosis), >=2-Burnout games 107 vs 108.

THE SCREEN (318,000 matches, 15 tables; two thermal-tier runs over disjoint seed halves, tallies summed; snapshot r39/, round.sh 05f3d8c1, cac-round 13545c71). League-shaped: v33-combined 20.4% (4,333), v30 same-round 20.2% (4,287), v34-release 20.3% (4,313). CF3-composition: v33 20.9, v34 20.8, v30 21.1. CF (tenth measurement): rado-replica 44.0, v11 20.4, v16 15.5, v17-value 10.8, macro-replica 9.4. Gauntlet pooled (within-class clause BINDS, Mage vs Mage): v33 2.21, v34 2.21, v30 same-round 2.39 - bleed 0.18 points, inside the 1-point allowance; GC/GD counts for v33 and v34 are identical (the release has almost no substrate in the gauntlet's Warrior monoculture, as Round 38 found for the clock). Table G baseline unmoved (v17-value 62.8).

VERDICT (the advance rule as amended, EE 842; within-class, so every clause binds). v33-combined: mechanism moved (release binds, W4 leg kept), shape kept, league-shaped beats the parent's same-round mark (20.4 vs 20.2), gauntlet clause passes. V33-COMBINED ADVANCES and is the advancing line; the next build's parent. The margin is named without varnish: the league-shaped beat is 46 matches in 21,200 (0.2 points), inside noise by any honest standard - the rule as written asks for a beat, and Round 38's v32 at exact parity did not advance under it; what carries this verdict beyond the 46 matches is that every independent read points the same way (traced wins +1.0, payload deaths -17.5 points of losses, W4 waste still 0, no measured cost anywhere). v34-release also beats its parent (20.3 vs 20.2) with the mechanism bound, and is dominated by v33 on every surface (league-shaped 4,313 < 4,333; traced wins 18.3 < 18.7; no W4 leg) - it closes as the ablation that prices the release's contribution: the release alone is worth ~+0.1-0.2 league-shaped points and the payload-death collapse; the combo adds the banked discount for free. Distance to the bar: league-shaped best is now 20.4% against the #1 contender's league mean 0.327 - about 12 points, third consecutive round at that distance; the gains are real and small, and the wall is the champions' survival, which the release dented but did not break.

THE FIRST HOSTED READ (study; harvest39.py over the observatory API; standings pulled live). v30-magehybrid was submitted at EE 846 (2026-11-26T08:47:18Z). In its first ~4.5 hours hosted: 57 episodes seated our policy (fields of 5 drawn from the division's ten members, ~3 episodes per ladder round; the ladder shows phext at 240 rounds vs 221 at submission, MMR 18.171 -> 18.278, rank #7 of 10 held). OUR HOSTED WIN SHARE: 8 of 57 = 14.0%, against the local league-shaped prediction of 20.3-20.4%. Splits: vs both champions in field 1/9 (11.1%), rado only 2/18 (11.1%), macromackie only 2/17 (11.8%), neither champion 3/13 (23.1%). Winner split of the 57: radogost 10, salvo 9, macromackie 8, us 8, A-aron 7. Read: at n=57 the interval is wide (roughly +/-9 points), but the direction is the one Rounds 29 and 33 taught - replica floors understate the real champions (the local room's rado is his scored rule at corpus strength; the real field also seats salvo, stilt, A-aron and others our league-shaped table does not), so the local mark overstates. This is SCREEN-class evidence about the prediction, and HOSTED evidence about v30: the two are kept separate. MOAT: exactly one registry action is legally supported - claim U25 ENTERED as Unknown/OPEN carrying this proposition and its first receipts (registry scroll updated: Unknown 15 -> 16). No existing claim's statement is tested by these receipts, and no transition is made; U20/U8/U10 still await hosted series only Will can authorize.

THERMAL RECORD OF THE ROUND. Pre-probe (idle): fleet 30.8-41.9 C, hub 63.6 C -> hub tiered to the hot set at slots 4, neon capped at 4 (sensorless). Load probes: hub 86.8 C during its chunk duty (a second reading between chunks: 49.8 C - chunk duty is bursty; the 86.8 stands as the peak reading and the protocol's response is already written: the hub's cap drops a tier in the protocol's next revision note, and its cooldown gate is 60 C); cool set under load 31-44 C across pre/post probes (the cool run phase lasted 132 s and outran the mid-run probe cadence - named here as an instrument gap: the protocol now wants a load probe at run start +60 s; this round's cool-set load numbers are pre/post only). Post-probe: every node back under 44 C; no node starts the next leg hot. No node overheated under the protocol's stop lines (90 C); the hub's 86.8 C peak is recorded as the round's thermal incident and the reason its tier tightens.

MACHINERY. Two concurrent round.sh invocations contend on the single egress proxy: the hot run's preflight took 45 s, the cool run's 428 s (serial preflight remains the largest block, and parallel runs multiply it - the continuous loop therefore runs ONE run at a time, split internally by tier). Run phases: cool tier 159,000 matches in 132 s = 1,205 matches/s (14 nodes, slots 8); hot tier 159,000 in 785 s = 203 matches/s (2 nodes, slots 4) - the thermal protocol's price, paid deliberately and recorded, not hidden. Fleet 16/18 both runs (halycon-vector, rock-mountain excluded at preflight, the standing pair). Incidents: (1) the first recorder launch passed bare bot filenames where record39.sh expects top2-relative paths and produced 300 empty recordings per arm - caught against the index (winners blank), recordings re-run with ../bots/ paths, 300/300 real; the sed-derived record39/trace39 scripts performed correctly thereafter, but the standing process fix (write fresh, never sed-derive) is re-asserted for the loop's legs. (2) A pkill pattern matched this session's own shell mid-recovery (the known self-match trap) - no work lost. (3) The hub tracer binary was already resident; a redundant scp of it failed harmlessly.

