## Per-surface findings

### S1. Leaderboard — anonymous, complete
`GET /v2/divisions/{DIV}/leaderboard` and `.../leaderboard/summary`:
**anon 200**. Exposes per member: rank, player_id, player_name,
**owner_name (first name + last initial of the human owner)**, MMR
(openskill score + sigma), mean_score/win_rate, rounds_played,
episode_wins, version_rounds_played (rounds played by the current
version), settling flag, and policy_label `name:vN` of the seated
champion. `rank_change` exists but read 0 for everyone in every pull we
have — it is a snapshot delta field, not a history.

### S2. League object — anonymous
`GET /v2/leagues/{LEAGUE}`: **anon 200**. Full league settings: openskill
(mu 25, sigma 8.33), round interval 15 min, 6 episodes/round, random_fill
with filler_policy for insufficient players, players_per_user 1, and
**`public_player_files: false`** — the league's own declaration that
player files are NOT public (see Boundary). Game created
2026-10-01T17:55:10Z; league is `public: true`, game_of_week.

### S3. Rounds — anonymous list, authenticated detail
`GET /v2/rounds?division_id={DIV}`: **anon 200** for the list (round ids,
numbers, entrant_attributions = membership + policy_version_id + player
id per seat). We paged 1,698 rounds back to round 2655
(2026-11-07T00:01Z) before the cursor chain ended — the public rounds
window in this pass reached ~19 days; the submissions listing (S5)
reaches deeper, to league creation. Per-round episode lists and episode
details are **auth-only** (anon 401).

### S4. Episodes — authenticated-any-user, effectively public evidence
- `GET /v2/coworlds/{COW}/episode-requests` (auth 200, anon 401): every
  non-private episode in the coworld, including other users' xp-request
  episodes (sampled: requester_user_id ≠ ours, seating the five champion
  policies; readable in full).
- `GET /v2/episode-requests/{ereq}` (auth 200): participants with
  policy_id, policy_name, **version number**, player_id, player_name,
  owner_name, per-seat scores, coworld version, variant, timestamps.
- Artifacts (auth 200, anon 401): `.../artifacts/replay` returns the full
  replay binary; `.../artifacts/logs` the game log. The `coworld
  episode-logs` CLI additionally downloads **per-seat agent logs for any
  seat** of league episodes — the programme already holds e.g.
  `logs/agents-aaron/` (A-aron's seat logs) and 507 fully traced league
  episodes. For this game-hosted BASIC format, the per-seat trace exposes
  the seat's complete play record (deck as dealt/played, every action) —
  behavior is public evidence by platform design; the policy FILE is not
  (S2, Boundary).
  **CORRECTION — 2026-11-26 (EE ~994): the per-seat agent-log claim
  in the bullet above is WRONG.** Competitor seat logs are NOT
  public. The field study (field.md §2) settled it directly: the
  download manifest serves `player_logs` only for seats the
  requester owns, and the direct route returns 403 "You do not own
  this policy" — verified against five rival policies. What IS
  public stands as audited elsewhere in this file: replays, game
  logs, the submissions corpus, and the anonymous leaderboard.
  Behavioral traces of competitors' games are available through
  the public replays, not through their seat logs; a seat's own
  logs are readable by its owner alone (so a seated champion's
  PRINT telemetry is a private channel, not a public one).
- Replay binaries also sit on a public S3 bucket
  (`softmax-public.s3.amazonaws.com/replays/<uuid>.replay`): anon range
  GET returned 206 — world-readable **if you have the URL**; URLs are
  only disclosed through auth endpoints.
- History depth: our harvested corpus spans 2026-11-24T14:42Z →
  2026-11-26T14:12Z (630 episode rows, 507 traced, 3,765 seat
  observations); sampled episode details confirm the same versions
  seated back to 2026-11-07 (S3 window).

### S5. League submissions — authenticated-any-user, the cadence record
`GET /v2/league-submissions?league_id={LEAGUE}&limit=500` (auth 200,
anon 401): **268 submissions, the league's complete submission history
from creation 2026-10-01T17:55Z to 2026-11-26T09:14Z** (limit is honored;
pagination params are ignored — one large-limit call returns all).
Each entry: submission id, status (all "placed"), created_at timestamp,
player (id, name, owner_name, avatar_url field), policy_version
(policy id + name, version number, version id), membership id,
auto_champion flag — and the submitter's own **`title`, `description`,
and `notes` text** (see Leak flags). This endpoint is the only public
surface with per-version timestamps, and it timestamps SUBMISSIONS,
not uploads.

### S6. Player profiles — no profile surface exists
`GET /v2/players/{ply}`, `/v2/players/{ply}/profile`, `/v2/users/{ply}`:
404 for anon and auth, for every roster member including us. There is no
public player page via the API: no bio, no join date, no cross-league
history, no trophy record. Everything knowable about a player is the
leaderboard row (S1) + their submission entries (S5, which carry an
avatar_url field — null in the samples read) + their episode seats (S4).

### S7. Forum and wiki — present, empty of competitor content
- Forum: `GET /v2/forums/Archers%20Warriors%20Mages.md` — "No posts."
- Wiki: `GET /v2/wikis/Archers%20Warriors%20Mages/pages.md` — two pages
  only, both game documentation (bot-writing quick start = play.md;
  main rules page). Wiki writes are restricted to league/game owners.
- No competitor has posted a strategy write-up, deck list, or comment in
  either surface.

### S8. Watch page
`https://softmax.com/watch?league={LEAGUE}` renders standings/episodes/
replays client-side from the same Observatory endpoints (the text fetch
shows only the loading shell). Nothing beyond S1/S4.

### S9. Off-platform web / GitHub
Exact-handle web searches ("radogost", "cac-macromackie", "docxology",
"eckstar" + softmax/Cards and Casters/GitHub) returned **no competitor
presence**: no repos, posts, or write-ups attributable to any roster
member. The game's own code is public by the game owner's choice
(github.com/softmax-universe/polyworld — engine + baseset), which is a
game surface, not a competitor disclosure. No competitor policy code was
found anywhere off-platform.

### S10. Standings history — NOT exposed; only self-harvested snapshots
`.../leaderboard/history` and `.../leaderboard/summary/history`: 404.
The platform exposes current state only (plus the inert rank_change
field). All history in this dossier comes from our own dated harvests:
2026-11-25 sweep files, EE 709 leaderboard, EE 885–909 round harvests,
and the S5 submission timestamps.

## Publish cadence — MEASURED (this section supersedes any "rapid publisher" framing)

Correction carried in from Will (EE ~913): a version number is a **stock**
(lifetime uploads to one policy name), never a rate. The flow, measured
from S5 submission timestamps + S4 episode version series + our dated
leaderboard observations, is: **an early-platform burst (Oct 1 – Nov 14),
then a league-wide freeze.** In the 12 days since 2026-11-14T17:00Z the
league has seen exactly **6 submissions: 3 are ours** (emise-cac-v6
11-24, emise-cac-v16 11-24, emise-cac-v30 11-26), 2 are Rohit's
(orch-7 v2 11-17, cac-rado v1 11-24), 1 is Eckstar's entry (11-26).
**Zero submissions from the current top 5 since 2026-11-14.**

### What the counters actually count
- Version numbers are **per policy (global to the policy name/ID), not
  per league**: A-aron submitted versions [3, 6, 53, 58, 109, 135, 142]
  — 135 of his 142 uploads were never submitted to this league at all
  (they exist for private xp-testing or other use; uploads are not
  publicly timestamped anywhere — `/v2/policy-versions/{id}` and
  `/v2/policies/{id}` return 404; the only public timestamps in the
  whole system are submission `created_at` and episode timestamps).
- Submitted-version series from episodes match the submission record
  exactly at every sampled point (14 sampled rounds, 2026-11-07 →
  2026-11-26): episodes show only the seated version, so episode data
  independently confirms first-appearance/last-change dates but cannot
  see unsubmitted uploads.
- Dated observations in our own record (state.md): radogost v166 and
  cac-macromackie v64 at EE 709 (2026-11-25), EE 885, 897, 900, 901,
  907, 909 and today — unchanged at every observation.

