# THE FIELD, UNDERSTOOD — Cards and Casters division, full study

_EE ~932–955, 2026-11-26. Will's directive: "we first need to understand the field."_
_League league_ad6dc809-4696-46f5-99a5-fc2b1c58d082 · division div_4d48d8bd-0a9c-40a8-be80-d02cdbba132f._

## Coverage — what this study actually rests on

- **Episodes: 10,242** — every completed episode reachable through the division's
  round chain, **2026-11-07T00:01Z → 2026-11-26T18:12Z**, seating any division
  member (past or present). The rounds cursor chain ends at 2026-11-07, so
  Oct 1 – Nov 6 episodes are **not reachable** through it; that boundary is
  stated, not smoothed over. (The league has run since 2026-10-01; the
  submissions corpus below covers the full span.)
- **Replays: 10,242 / 10,242 downloaded. Traces: 10,242 / 10,242 traced,
  10,242 / 10,242 hash-verified** (v3 tracer, ~/polyworld-v3 at 78c6a620^ on
  aletheia-core; the hub's v4 tree rejects v3 replays). **155 distinct policy
  versions profiled** from traces.
- **Game logs: 4,336 downloaded. Player (agent) logs: 468 files — all of them
  ours** (see §6; competitor player logs are ownership-gated, a correction to
  our earlier audit).
- **Submissions: all 268 read whole** (titles/descriptions/notes), full text in
  `field/submissions-by-competitor.json`, synthesis in
  `field/submissions-synthesis.md`.
- Data files: `field/index-field.jsonl` (episode index), `field/matrix.json`
  (full pairwise matrix, all 155 versions), `field/dynamics.json`,
  `field/profiles.json` (per-policy trace profiles), `field/v30-decomp.json`,
  `field/rows/` (per-episode API records), `field/replays/`, `field/traces/`,
  `field/agentlogs/`, `field/gamelogs/`.

## The three largest corrections to our previous field picture

1. **The field is not ten builds — it is a graveyard of ~155 versions, and the
   champions' lineages crossed all three classes.** radogost got to Warrior
   v166 through a control **Mage** (v91: 877 games, 0.287, median death turn
   56) and an **Archer** (v121: 222 games, 0.320, Post/Gift). Andrew Brower's
   best build ever was a **Mage** (stilt v21, 0.346) — his seated Warrior v30
   (0.199) is what remained after his Mage line collapsed (v24: 0.050) and he
   pivoted. Our top-2 corpus treated class as identity; the field treats
   class as a phase.
2. **Competitors' per-seat agent logs are NOT public.** The download-manifest
   serves player_logs only for seats the requester owns; the direct route
   returns 403 "You do not own this policy" (verified against five rival
   policies), and the OpenAPI schema states ownership applies. Our earlier
   public-information audit's claim that any seat's agent log is readable is
   **wrong** and is corrected here. The only readable player logs are our own
   (468 files: v6/v16/v30 seats) — and every one is the bare 49-byte runtime
   text. The field's talk behavior is *unobservable*, not "silent" (§6).
3. **macromackie — not radogost — is the wall for us, and the local tables
   hide it.** Hosted, v30 scores **0.058 with macro in the room (n=52) vs
   0.258 without him (n=62)**. Our macro-replica's Mage family converts at
   0.036 locally against his real 0.307–0.403, so league-shaped tables have
   been grading candidates against a champion at roughly one-tenth strength
   in the seat that matters most. Rado is beatable (0.137 with / 0.190
   without); macro at full strength is the distance to the bar.

---

## 1. Profile cards — the ten seated members

Shares are full-window hosted episode win shares (index, Nov 7–26) unless a
trace figure is named. "atk_low" = fraction of hero attacks aimed at the
lowest-life living opponent; "scored" = agreement with rado's rule
(life − 2·boardPower + boardCount) for comparison.

### #1 Andre von Auto — radogost:v166 — Warrior — 4,354 g, **0.394**
- Deck: stock Warrior with exactly one swap (Duel out, Hail of Arrows in) —
  confirmed at full scale (single deck variant in 4,354 games).
- Targeting: atk_low 0.731, scored-rule agreement 0.778 (his own rule, from
  R33). 1,820 Hail casts at median opposing board 16 / 13 one-tough — he
  holds Hail for genuinely full boards. Dies first only 7.5%; median death
  turn 26. Kills: salvo 695, A-aron 482, macro 463.
- Lineage (traced): Mage control v91 (0.287, death-turn median 56) →
  Archer v121 (0.320) → Mage v124 with Post/Gift (0.271) → … → Warrior v166.
  Version stock 166 over Oct 1 – Nov 14; **101 submissions, zero prose**
  (submissions census A-1). Silent since 2026-11-14.

### #2 macromackie — cac-macromackie:v64 — Mage/Warrior deck-selecting — 4,592 g, **0.307**
- Five (class, deck) combos; Mage 3,237 g / Warrior 1,355 g. Main Mage shell:
  12× Archer-class trinkets (the C2 discount engine), Post 4,682 casts with
  Post-with-minion 1.000. atk_low 0.827 — he focuses the lowest-life seat
  harder than his reputation for spread play suggests. Median board max 10.
- **Self-kills: 272 of his losses end during his own actions** (his own
