## 2. Notable historical seats (in-window, no longer seated)

- **volley:v2 (Fletcher) — Archer — 415 g, 0.188.** A real Archer build
  plays in this field: Mage-class trinkets ×6, Sniper/Sharpshooter, Bolt
  540, Post 524 (pwm 1.0), Hail 401 at board median 15, Reload 481.
  atk_low 0.178 (spread fire). This — not daf — is the field's Archer
  evidence; it predates the freeze and seats no longer.
- **greenshank:v30 (Andrew B) — Mage control — 661 g, 0.306.** Ooze 3,594
  plays, death-turn median 58. In era 1 this shell family (with stilt v21
  and rado v91) *was* the top of the field.
- **AWM Baseline:v2 (platform seed) — Warrior — 655 g, 0.069.** Stock deck
  played loosely (Footsoldier 6,875 plays = it floods and stalls; death
  median 54). Not a filler — a seed account's policy, era-1 only.
- **radogost:v91 / stilt:v21 / relh deckwarden** — the era-1 control-Mage
  cluster: death-turn medians 56–58, shares 0.29–0.35 in their window.
  Era-1 games ran roughly **twice as long** as era-3 games.

## 3. Filler cards — the four random_fill policies

All four seat only in the early window (282 games total, Nov 7–13 era);
with ten members, random_fill almost never fires — **zero of v30's 114
episodes seat a filler**, and none seat after the field filled.

| Policy | Class | Games | Share | Signature |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| AWM Warrior Reference:v1 | Warrior | 69 | 0.029 | stock deck, loose play (Footsoldier 657) |
| AWM Mage Reference:v1 | Mage | 55 | 0.036 | Morphosis/Bouncer control shell |
| AWM Archer Reference:v1 | Archer | 84 | 0.024 | native Archer: Ambusher/Sniper/Wildfire, Hail 126 |
| AWM Archer Warrior Reference:v1 | Archer | 74 | 0.027 | Archer hero, Warrior bodies (Warrior ×227 plays), Hail 110 |

True filler strength is 0.024–0.036 — an order below the weakest member.
Any table that seats fillers as a routine fifth seat is grading against a
field that does not exist.

## 4. Our seat in the field — v30 decomposition

114 hosted episodes, 19 wins, **0.167**; all 114 traced. Local league-shaped
read at advance time: ~20.3–20.4%. Gap ≈ **3.6–3.7 points**, decomposed:

- **Composition — macromackie (dominant term).** With macro seated: **0.058
  (n=52)**; without: **0.258 (n=62)**. He wins 21 of our 114 episodes and is
  the killer in 26 of 95 losses. Hosted rooms seat him at member frequency;
  local tables seat the macro-replica, whose Mage family converts at 0.036
  vs his real 0.307+ — the replica infidelity on this one seat is worth
  roughly the whole gap. (Replica-vs-real E1 gap measured independently in
  improvement tracking: −0.234 mean — the two instruments agree on sign and
  scale.)
- **Composition — the dead seat (offsets the other way).** With daf seated:
  0.200 (n=45); without: 0.145 (n=69) — **+5.5 points of our hosted share is
  the bye**. Local tables don't seat daf; this term makes hosted *easier*,
  meaning the macro term above is understated by roughly the same amount.
- **Composition — rado:** 0.137 with (n=51) / 0.190 without (n=63): −5.3
  points when the #1 is present, at roughly member frequency locally too —
  this term is priced approximately right by the rado-replica (his replica
  floor is, if anything, strong).
- **Fillers: zero episodes.** No component.
- **Seat position:** seat 0: 7/31 (0.226); seat 1: 1/20 (0.050); seat 2:
  2/19; seat 3: 7/23 (0.304); seat 4: 2/21. Small cells — named as noise,
  not a lever, until n grows.
- **Death causes (95 losses traced):** macro 26, salvo 20, A-aron 19,
  rado 11, **SELF-Burnout 6 (6.3%)**, stilt 5, cac-rado 5, eckstar 3.
  Median death turn **26** — hosted deaths come ~3.5 turns earlier than the
  lineage's local autopsy median (~29.5): the real field kills faster than
  our tables do, consistent with the champions being under-strength locally.
- **Engine/hosted differences:** no component found. All 10,242 traces
  hash-verify against the local v3 engine — the hosted game *is* this
  engine. The residual after composition is replica infidelity (macro
  first, then the un-replicated salvo/A-aron/richard seats), not physics.
- **Unmeasurable, named:** per-decision divergence of hosted v30 from its
  local twin on identical seeds (hosted seeds are not exposed, so a paired
  comparison cannot be run); the winner's-hand term (winner hands are
  visible in replays — extractable, not yet harvested).

