# D11 lethal-fix — v39-lethalfix (repair pass leg 2, EE 993–994)

Will's direction: "we've made mistakes, find and fix them." This leg
builds the redesign audit's D11 fix and proves or refutes that it
moves the W1 spared-executioner metric. **Nothing uploaded, nothing
submitted — a ship of any fix is Will's word.**

## The defect — source-proven, exactly as the audit described

The audit (design-choices-v2.md, D11) claimed the lethal test reads
`enemyLife` — the next seat's life — instead of the targeted hero's.
Verified verbatim at both ends before building:

- Engine (hub clone `~/polyworld/games/cac/core/bots.nim`):
  `# With more than two players, the script's "enemy" is the next
  living one.` — `let enemy = game.nextPlayer(player)`, and per
  decision `setData(ids[DataEnemyLife], game.players[enemy].life)`.
  So the `enemyLife` data slot IS the next living seat's life.
- Chassis (`bots/v38-gift2.bas`, `swing:`, the k = 2 hero branch;
  the swing's target owner is `o` = `attackChoiceOwner(id, c)`):
  line 710 was `IF myPower >= enemyLife THEN value = 100`. The same
  branch already prices the actual target two lines below (the v32
  W4 rule: `playerLife(o) <= burnBand AND myPower < playerLife(o)`),
  so `playerLife(o)` is the correct, in-scope expression.

The audit's code-shape description matched the file exactly; no
improvisation was needed.

## The build

Generator: `top2/make_v39.py` (make_v37.py precedent — source hash
asserted, anchor asserted exactly once and inside the k = 2 branch,
output asserted to differ on exactly one line).

- Source: `bots/v38-gift2.bas`, sha256
  `edd8f49ab7dcd3e383114f9b1339c0d5242ab37ce5b655b09eb57cc1a2139537`
  (the shipped/screened bytes; hub `~/t41g/gift2.bas` verified
  byte-identical, so the existing f41 gift2 traces ARE the v38 arm).
- Hunk H-lethal (line 710, the only differing line):
  `-  IF myPower >= enemyLife THEN value = 100`
  `+  IF myPower >= playerLife(o) THEN value = 100`
- Candidate: `bots/v39-lethalfix.bas`, 49,139 B, sha256
  `682b46954af53ec5c44ccd83545fb4b8b13a379fb02039fbfbc42627aba0cc98`
- The embedded phext volume, libphext include, deck, thetas and
  every other decision are byte-identical to v38 (the one-line diff
  is the whole diff; the remaining `enemyLife` occurrence in v39 is
  the line-25 slot-list comment, not decision logic).

